IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb4-common`
IMPORT `cb4-amendment`
IMPORT `cb4-amalgamation`
IMPORT `cb4-continuance`
IMPORT `cb4-borrowing-sale`
IMPORT `cb4-dissent`
IMPORT `cb4-reorg-arrangement`
IMPORT `cb4-going-private`
IMPORT `cb4-takeover`
IMPORT `cb4-after-dissolution`
IMPORT `cb4-liquidator`
IMPORT `cb4-court-liquidation`
IMPORT `cb4-dissolution`
IMPORT `cb4-seat`

-- Worked cases for cb4-seat.l4: at least one per question, each in the facts a real person in the seat
-- would state. Every expected value is written from the text of the section named beside it, before
-- the run, never copied from the encoding's output. A case outside the encoding asserts the explicit
-- not-covered value (NOTHING or a named constructor).

§ `Cases -- the seat of a founder, director or shareholder (Parts XV to XVIII)`

§§ `Changing the articles (Part XV, ss 173 to 180)`

-- Case: Priya and Sam run Maple Leaf Widgets Corp.; they want to rename it. 200 of the 300 votes cast
-- favour (two-thirds exactly): the special resolution passes (s 2(1)), and no class has a separate vote.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation validly adopted this change to its articles` WITH `the change` IS `to change the name (s 173(1)(a))`, `our stated capital is set out in the articles` IS FALSE, `the change in the number of directors complies with sections 107 and 112` IS FALSE, `the Act permits that provision to be in the articles` IS FALSE, `votes cast in favour` IS 200, `votes cast against` IS 100, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE, `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS TRUE
-- The same vote, but a class with a separate vote did not approve: not adopted (s 176(6)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation validly adopted this change to its articles` WITH `the change` IS `to change the name (s 173(1)(a))`, `our stated capital is set out in the articles` IS FALSE, `the change in the number of directors complies with sections 107 and 112` IS FALSE, `the Act permits that provision to be in the articles` IS FALSE, `votes cast in favour` IS 200, `votes cast against` IS 100, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE, `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS FALSE)
-- A change s 173(1) does not list is not authorized by it, whatever the vote.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation validly adopted this change to its articles` WITH `the change` IS `a change that s 173(1) does not list`, `our stated capital is set out in the articles` IS TRUE, `the change in the number of directors complies with sections 107 and 112` IS TRUE, `the Act permits that provision to be in the articles` IS TRUE, `votes cast in favour` IS 300, `votes cast against` IS 0, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS TRUE, `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS TRUE)
-- A reduction of stated capital where the stated capital is not set out in the articles: paragraph (f) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation validly adopted this change to its articles` WITH `the change` IS `to reduce or increase stated capital set out in the articles (s 173(1)(f))`, `our stated capital is set out in the articles` IS FALSE, `the change in the number of directors complies with sections 107 and 112` IS FALSE, `the Act permits that provision to be in the articles` IS FALSE, `votes cast in favour` IS 300, `votes cast against` IS 0, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE, `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS TRUE)
-- A resolution signed by every shareholder entitled to vote passes with no votes cast.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation validly adopted this change to its articles` WITH `the change` IS `to change the province of the registered office (s 173(1)(b))`, `our stated capital is set out in the articles` IS FALSE, `the change in the number of directors complies with sections 107 and 112` IS FALSE, `the Act permits that provision to be in the articles` IS FALSE, `votes cast in favour` IS 0, `votes cast against` IS 0, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS TRUE, `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS TRUE

-- Case: the shareholders' resolution says the directors may revoke it; nothing has been done under it yet.
#ASSERT `May the directors revoke the shareholders' special resolution without asking us again` WITH `the resolution authorized the directors to revoke it` IS TRUE, `the resolution has been acted on` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors revoke the shareholders' special resolution without asking us again` WITH `the resolution authorized the directors to revoke it` IS TRUE, `the resolution has been acted on` IS TRUE)

-- Case: 6543210 Canada Inc. wants a name in words; the directors change it themselves.
#ASSERT `May the directors alone change our corporation's number name to a name in words` WITH `our corporation's name is a designating number` IS TRUE, `the new name is a name in words` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors alone change our corporation's number name to a name in words` WITH `our corporation's name is a designating number` IS FALSE, `the new name is a name in words` IS TRUE)

-- Case: a distributing corporation with many shareholders limits the issue and transfer of its shares to
-- Canadian residents; 201 of 300 votes (more than two-thirds) are in favour.
#ASSERT `May my corporation put this constraint on who can hold its shares` WITH `our corporation is a distributing corporation` IS TRUE, `issued shares remain outstanding` IS TRUE, `those shares are held by more than one person` IS TRUE, `the constraint` IS `on the issue or transfer of shares to persons who are not resident Canadians (s 174(1)(a))`, `the law concerned is prescribed` IS FALSE, `the amendment follows the regulations` IS TRUE, `shares of the affected class or series are outstanding` IS FALSE, `those shares are already constrained` IS FALSE, `votes cast in favour` IS 201, `votes cast against` IS 99, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE
-- A private corporation (not a distributing corporation) may not.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation put this constraint on who can hold its shares` WITH `our corporation is a distributing corporation` IS FALSE, `issued shares remain outstanding` IS TRUE, `those shares are held by more than one person` IS TRUE, `the constraint` IS `on the issue or transfer of shares to persons who are not resident Canadians (s 174(1)(a))`, `the law concerned is prescribed` IS FALSE, `the amendment follows the regulations` IS TRUE, `shares of the affected class or series are outstanding` IS FALSE, `those shares are already constrained` IS FALSE, `votes cast in favour` IS 201, `votes cast against` IS 99, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE)
-- The licences/benefits constraint cannot be put on an outstanding class that is not already constrained (s 174(2)).
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation put this constraint on who can hold its shares` WITH `our corporation is a distributing corporation` IS TRUE, `issued shares remain outstanding` IS TRUE, `those shares are held by more than one person` IS TRUE, `the constraint` IS `on issue, transfer or ownership to qualify for licences, permits, grants or benefits by a level of Canadian ownership or control (s 174(1)(c))`, `the law concerned is prescribed` IS TRUE, `the amendment follows the regulations` IS TRUE, `shares of the affected class or series are outstanding` IS TRUE, `those shares are already constrained` IS FALSE, `votes cast in favour` IS 201, `votes cast against` IS 99, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE)

-- Case: the corporation caps one holder's shares to protect a grant tied to 51 per cent Canadian ownership.
#ASSERT `May my corporation cap or bar a person's ownership of its shares` WITH `the cap or bar is made under the licences, permits, grants or benefits constraint` IS TRUE, `the person's ownership would adversely affect that level` IS TRUE, `that level is specified in the articles and meets the level the Act refers to` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation cap or bar a person's ownership of its shares` WITH `the cap or bar is made under the licences, permits, grants or benefits constraint` IS TRUE, `the person's ownership would adversely affect that level` IS FALSE, `that level is specified in the articles and meets the level the Act refers to` IS TRUE)

-- Case: the corporation removes its non-resident constraint by a vote of 150 to 140: two-thirds not reached.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation change or remove a constraint on its shares by special resolution` WITH `our corporation is a distributing corporation` IS TRUE, `issued shares remain outstanding` IS TRUE, `those shares are held by more than one person` IS TRUE, `votes cast in favour` IS 150, `votes cast against` IS 140, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May my corporation change or remove a constraint on its shares by special resolution` WITH `our corporation is a distributing corporation` IS TRUE, `issued shares remain outstanding` IS TRUE, `those shares are held by more than one person` IS TRUE, `votes cast in favour` IS 280, `votes cast against` IS 10, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE

-- Case: a share was issued to a non-resident in breach of the constraint; nothing else is wrong with it.
#ASSERT (`Is an issue or transfer of shares still valid although the corporation did not follow s 174` WITH `the only defect is not following section 174 or the regulations` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Outside the encoding: another defect as well, which s 174(7) does not decide.
#ASSERT (`Is an issue or transfer of shares still valid although the corporation did not follow s 174` WITH `the only defect is not following section 174 or the regulations` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case: Amira, a director, asks to put a proposal to the next annual meeting.
#ASSERT `May I make a proposal to amend the articles` WITH `I am a director` IS TRUE, `I am a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting` IS FALSE, `my proposal follows section 137` IS TRUE
-- Case: Ben holds non-voting shares only and is not a director.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I make a proposal to amend the articles` WITH `I am a director` IS FALSE, `I am a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting` IS FALSE, `my proposal follows section 137` IS TRUE)

-- Case: the notice sets out the amendment and the amendment gives a right to dissent, but the notice says nothing of it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the notice of the meeting say what the Act requires about a proposed amendment` WITH `the notice sets out the amendment` IS TRUE, `shareholders have a right to dissent from it` IS TRUE, `the notice states that right` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the notice of the meeting say what the Act requires about a proposed amendment` WITH `the notice sets out the amendment` IS TRUE, `shareholders have a right to dissent from it` IS FALSE, `the notice states that right` IS FALSE
-- The same omission: the amendment is not invalid for that reason alone (s 175(2)).
#ASSERT (`Is the amendment invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` WITH `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the omission does not make the action invalid`
#ASSERT (`Is the amendment invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` WITH `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the Act does not say whether the omission makes the action invalid`

-- Case: the corporation will create a new class ranking equal to Dina's class: Dina's class has a separate vote.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to vote separately, as a holder of a class of shares, on this proposed amendment` WITH `what the amendment does to my class` IS `the creation of a new class equal or superior to the class (s 176(1)(e))`, `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS FALSE, `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS FALSE, `the amendment only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS FALSE
-- The new class is a constrained class otherwise equal to hers: deemed not equal or superior (s 176(3)): no separate vote.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to vote separately, as a holder of a class of shares, on this proposed amendment` WITH `what the amendment does to my class` IS `the creation of a new class equal or superior to the class (s 176(1)(e))`, `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS FALSE, `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS TRUE, `the amendment only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS FALSE)
-- Her class's rights are cut: the articles cannot take the vote away for that case (c).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to vote separately, as a holder of a class of shares, on this proposed amendment` WITH `what the amendment does to my class` IS `a change to the rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached to the shares of the class (s 176(1)(c))`, `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS TRUE, `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS FALSE, `the amendment only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS FALSE
-- Outside the encoding: an amendment with no effect s 176(1) lists.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to vote separately, as a holder of a class of shares, on this proposed amendment` WITH `what the amendment does to my class` IS `no effect that s 176(1) lists`, `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS FALSE, `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS FALSE, `the amendment only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS FALSE)

-- Case: Eli holds Series 2 of Class A; only Series 2 is hit differently.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to vote separately, as a holder of a series of shares, on this proposed amendment` WITH `my shares are a series of a class` IS TRUE, `my series is affected differently` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to vote separately, as a holder of a series of shares, on this proposed amendment` WITH `my shares are a series of a class` IS TRUE, `my series is affected differently` IS FALSE)

-- Case: Fay holds non-voting shares of a class that has a separate vote: she votes with her class anyway.
#ASSERT `Can I vote separately with my class or series although my shares carry no other vote` WITH `I am entitled to a separate vote under section 176(1)` IS TRUE, `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS FALSE

-- Case: Class B (the holders of my class) voted 60 for and 40 against: two-thirds not reached.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my class or series approved the amendment by special resolution` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 60, `votes cast against` IS 40, `the resolution was signed by every holder of the class or series` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Has my class or series approved the amendment by special resolution` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 70, `votes cast against` IS 30, `the resolution was signed by every holder of the class or series` IS FALSE

-- Case: the amendment is adopted and not revoked: the corporation must send the articles of amendment.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation now send articles of amendment to the Director` WITH `the amendment has been adopted` IS TRUE, `the directors revoked the resolution` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation now send articles of amendment to the Director` WITH `the amendment has been adopted` IS TRUE, `the directors revoked the resolution` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Do the rules on reducing stated capital apply to this amendment` WITH `the amendment reduces stated capital or requires it to be reduced` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Director give my corporation a certificate of amendment` WITH `the Director has received our articles of amendment` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director give my corporation a certificate of amendment` WITH `the Director has received our articles of amendment` IS FALSE)

-- Case: the certificate of amendment shows 10 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Has the amendment taken effect on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 10, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 10
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the amendment taken effect on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 10, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 9)

-- Case: a lawsuit against the corporation was already under way when the articles were amended.
#ASSERT (`Does the amendment of the articles affect a claim, liability or proceeding that already exists` WITH `the matter is an existing claim, liability or proceeding involving the corporation or its directors or officers` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Does the amendment of the articles affect a claim, liability or proceeding that already exists` WITH `the matter is an existing claim, liability or proceeding involving the corporation or its directors or officers` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case: s 180.
#ASSERT (`Must the directors restate our articles` WITH `the Director has reasonably directed the directors to restate the articles` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the directors must restate the articles`
#ASSERT (`Must the directors restate our articles` WITH `the Director has reasonably directed the directors to restate the articles` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the directors may restate the articles at any time and are not required to`
#ASSERT `Must we send the restated articles to the Director` WITH `the articles have been restated` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Director give us a restated certificate of incorporation` WITH `the Director has received our restated articles` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Do the restated articles replace our earlier articles on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the restated certificate` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 2
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the restated articles replace our earlier articles on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the restated certificate` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)

§§ `Amalgamating with another corporation (Part XV, ss 181 to 186.1)`

-- Case: Northern Lumber Ltd. and Prairie Mills Ltd. want to amalgamate. Two corporations: allowed (s 181).
#ASSERT `Can my corporation amalgamate with other corporations` WITH `the number of corporations that propose to amalgamate` IS 2
-- A corporation alone cannot amalgamate with itself.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my corporation amalgamate with other corporations` WITH `the number of corporations that propose to amalgamate` IS 1)

-- Case: their agreement states everything; some shares are not converted and the agreement says what those holders get.
#ASSERT `Does our amalgamation agreement contain everything the Act requires` WITH `every corporation proposing to amalgamate has signed the agreement` IS TRUE, `it sets out the provisions that section 6 requires in articles` IS TRUE, `it names and gives the address of each proposed director` IS TRUE, `it sets out how shares are converted` IS TRUE, `some shares are not converted into securities of the amalgamated corporation` IS TRUE, `it sets out what those holders receive instead` IS TRUE, `it sets out how fractional shares are paid for in money` IS TRUE, `it states whether the by-laws are those of an amalgamating corporation` IS TRUE, `the by-laws are not those of an amalgamating corporation` IS TRUE, `it includes a copy of the proposed by-laws` IS TRUE, `it sets out the arrangements to perfect the amalgamation and manage the new corporation` IS TRUE
-- The agreement does not say what the unconverted shares' holders receive: not compliant.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our amalgamation agreement contain everything the Act requires` WITH `every corporation proposing to amalgamate has signed the agreement` IS TRUE, `it sets out the provisions that section 6 requires in articles` IS TRUE, `it names and gives the address of each proposed director` IS TRUE, `it sets out how shares are converted` IS TRUE, `some shares are not converted into securities of the amalgamated corporation` IS TRUE, `it sets out what those holders receive instead` IS FALSE, `it sets out how fractional shares are paid for in money` IS TRUE, `it states whether the by-laws are those of an amalgamating corporation` IS TRUE, `the by-laws are not those of an amalgamating corporation` IS FALSE, `it includes a copy of the proposed by-laws` IS FALSE, `it sets out the arrangements to perfect the amalgamation and manage the new corporation` IS TRUE)

-- Case: Northern holds 40 per cent of Prairie's shares; the agreement cancels them without repaying capital.
#ASSERT `Does our agreement deal properly with shares one amalgamating corporation holds in another` WITH `one amalgamating corporation holds shares of another` IS TRUE, `the agreement cancels those shares without repaying capital` IS TRUE, `the agreement converts those shares` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our agreement deal properly with shares one amalgamating corporation holds in another` WITH `one amalgamating corporation holds shares of another` IS TRUE, `the agreement cancels those shares without repaying capital` IS FALSE, `the agreement converts those shares` IS TRUE)

-- Case: the directors must put the agreement to a meeting; not if it is a short-form amalgamation.
#ASSERT `Must the directors put the amalgamation agreement to the shareholders at a meeting` WITH `it is an amalgamation under the agreement of section 182 and not a short-form one` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the directors put the amalgamation agreement to the shareholders at a meeting` WITH `it is an amalgamation under the agreement of section 182 and not a short-form one` IS FALSE)

-- Case: the notice went to every shareholder with a summary but did not mention the right to dissent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the notice of the amalgamation meeting say what the Act requires` WITH `the notice complies with section 135` IS TRUE, `the notice goes to every shareholder of every amalgamating corporation` IS TRUE, `a copy or summary of the agreement is with the notice` IS TRUE, `shareholders have the right to dissent` IS TRUE, `the notice states that right` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the notice of the amalgamation meeting say what the Act requires` WITH `the notice complies with section 135` IS TRUE, `the notice goes to every shareholder of every amalgamating corporation` IS TRUE, `a copy or summary of the agreement is with the notice` IS TRUE, `shareholders have the right to dissent` IS TRUE, `the notice states that right` IS TRUE
#ASSERT (`Is the amalgamation invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` WITH `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the omission does not make the action invalid`
#ASSERT (`Is the amalgamation invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` WITH `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the Act does not say whether the omission makes the action invalid`

-- Case: Gita holds non-voting preferred shares. She still votes on the amalgamation (s 183(3)).
#ASSERT `Can I vote on the amalgamation although my shares carry no other vote` WITH `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I vote on the amalgamation although my shares carry no other vote` WITH `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS TRUE

-- Case: the agreement changes the rights attached to Gita's class: her class votes separately.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to vote separately, with my class or series, on the amalgamation agreement` WITH `what the agreement does to my class` IS `a change to the rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached to the shares of the class (s 176(1)(c))`, `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS FALSE, `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS FALSE, `the agreement only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS FALSE, `my shares are a series of a class` IS FALSE, `my series is affected differently` IS FALSE
-- Outside the encoding: an agreement provision that s 176(1) does not list gives no separate vote.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to vote separately, with my class or series, on the amalgamation agreement` WITH `what the agreement does to my class` IS `no effect that s 176(1) lists`, `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS FALSE, `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS FALSE, `the agreement only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS FALSE, `my shares are a series of a class` IS FALSE, `my series is affected differently` IS FALSE)

-- Case: Northern's vote is 2,000 for and 1,000 against: exactly two-thirds, and no class has a separate vote.
#ASSERT `Have my corporation's shareholders approved the amalgamation agreement` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 2000, `votes cast against` IS 1000, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE, `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have my corporation's shareholders approved the amalgamation agreement` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 1999, `votes cast against` IS 1001, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE, `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Have my corporation's shareholders approved the amalgamation agreement` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 2000, `votes cast against` IS 1000, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE, `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is the amalgamation agreement adopted by all the amalgamating corporations` WITH `my corporation's shareholders have approved it` IS TRUE, `the shareholders of every other amalgamating corporation have approved it` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the amalgamation agreement adopted by all the amalgamating corporations` WITH `my corporation's shareholders have approved it` IS TRUE, `the shareholders of every other amalgamating corporation have approved it` IS FALSE)

-- Case: the agreement lets the directors walk away before the certificate, and none has issued.
#ASSERT `May the directors terminate the amalgamation agreement even though the shareholders approved it` WITH `the agreement says the directors may terminate it before the certificate` IS TRUE, `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors terminate the amalgamation agreement even though the shareholders approved it` WITH `the agreement says the directors may terminate it before the certificate` IS TRUE, `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors terminate the amalgamation agreement even though the shareholders approved it` WITH `the agreement says the directors may terminate it before the certificate` IS FALSE, `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued` IS FALSE)

-- Case: a parent and its wholly-held subsidiary amalgamate on directors' resolutions alone.
#ASSERT `Can a holding corporation and its subsidiaries amalgamate by directors' resolutions alone` WITH `we are a holding corporation and one or more of its subsidiaries` IS TRUE, `each corporation's directors approved by resolution` IS TRUE, `each subsidiary's issued shares are all held within the group` IS TRUE, `the resolutions cancel the subsidiaries' shares without repaying capital` IS TRUE, `the resolutions keep the holding corporation's articles` IS TRUE, `the resolutions issue no securities and keep the holding corporation's stated capital` IS TRUE
-- A minority shareholder still holds some of the subsidiary: not allowed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a holding corporation and its subsidiaries amalgamate by directors' resolutions alone` WITH `we are a holding corporation and one or more of its subsidiaries` IS TRUE, `each corporation's directors approved by resolution` IS TRUE, `each subsidiary's issued shares are all held within the group` IS FALSE, `the resolutions cancel the subsidiaries' shares without repaying capital` IS TRUE, `the resolutions keep the holding corporation's articles` IS TRUE, `the resolutions issue no securities and keep the holding corporation's stated capital` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Can wholly-owned subsidiaries of one holding company amalgamate by directors' resolutions alone` WITH `we are wholly-owned subsidiaries of the same holding body corporate` IS TRUE, `each corporation's directors approved by resolution` IS TRUE, `the resolutions cancel all but one subsidiary's shares without repaying capital` IS TRUE, `the resolutions keep the articles of the subsidiary not cancelled` IS TRUE, `the resolutions add the cancelled subsidiaries' stated capital to the other's` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can wholly-owned subsidiaries of one holding company amalgamate by directors' resolutions alone` WITH `we are wholly-owned subsidiaries of the same holding body corporate` IS FALSE, `each corporation's directors approved by resolution` IS TRUE, `the resolutions cancel all but one subsidiary's shares without repaying capital` IS TRUE, `the resolutions keep the articles of the subsidiary not cancelled` IS TRUE, `the resolutions add the cancelled subsidiaries' stated capital to the other's` IS TRUE)

-- Case: sending the articles.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation now send articles of amalgamation to the Director` WITH `the amalgamation was adopted under section 183` IS TRUE, `the amalgamation was approved under section 184` IS FALSE, `the directors terminated the agreement` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation now send articles of amalgamation to the Director` WITH `the amalgamation was adopted under section 183` IS TRUE, `the amalgamation was approved under section 184` IS FALSE, `the directors terminated the agreement` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Have we sent the articles of amalgamation to the Director as the Act requires` WITH `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS TRUE, `the documents under sections 19 and 106 went with them` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have we sent the articles of amalgamation to the Director as the Act requires` WITH `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS TRUE, `the documents under sections 19 and 106 went with them` IS FALSE)

-- Case: the declaration says all is well and creditors have been given notice, with no objection.
#ASSERT `Does the statutory declaration attached to our articles of amalgamation meet the Act` WITH `a director or an officer of each amalgamating corporation made a statutory declaration` IS TRUE, `we can pay our liabilities as they fall due` IS TRUE, `the assets will be worth at least the liabilities and stated capital` IS TRUE, `no creditor will be prejudiced` IS FALSE, `adequate notice has been given to known creditors` IS TRUE, `no creditor objects on grounds that are not frivolous or vexatious` IS TRUE, `the Director is satisfied` IS TRUE
-- A creditor does object on a serious ground and creditors may be prejudiced: not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the statutory declaration attached to our articles of amalgamation meet the Act` WITH `a director or an officer of each amalgamating corporation made a statutory declaration` IS TRUE, `we can pay our liabilities as they fall due` IS TRUE, `the assets will be worth at least the liabilities and stated capital` IS TRUE, `no creditor will be prejudiced` IS FALSE, `adequate notice has been given to known creditors` IS TRUE, `no creditor objects on grounds that are not frivolous or vexatious` IS FALSE, `the Director is satisfied` IS TRUE)

-- Case: a supplier is owed exactly 1,000 dollars: no written notice is required; one owed 1,000.01 must be told.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must we send a written notice of the amalgamation to this creditor` WITH `the creditor's claim against us in dollars` IS 1000)
#ASSERT `Must we send a written notice of the amalgamation to this creditor` WITH `the creditor's claim against us in dollars` IS 1000.01
#ASSERT `Have we given our creditors adequate notice of the amalgamation` WITH `we sent a written notice to every known creditor with a claim over $1,000` IS TRUE, `we published a notice once in a newspaper at the registered office's place` IS TRUE, `we gave reasonable notice in each province where we carry on business` IS TRUE, `each notice says we intend to amalgamate with the named corporations` IS TRUE, `each notice says a creditor may object within thirty days` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have we given our creditors adequate notice of the amalgamation` WITH `we sent a written notice to every known creditor with a claim over $1,000` IS TRUE, `we published a notice once in a newspaper at the registered office's place` IS FALSE, `we gave reasonable notice in each province where we carry on business` IS TRUE, `each notice says we intend to amalgamate with the named corporations` IS TRUE, `each notice says a creditor may object within thirty days` IS TRUE)
-- Notice dated 10 March 2026: thirty days from that date ends on 9 April 2026.
#ASSERT (`What is the last day on which a creditor may object to the amalgamation` WITH `the date of our notice to creditors` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 9

#ASSERT `Must the Director give us a certificate of amalgamation` WITH `the Director has received our articles of amalgamation` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director give us a certificate of amalgamation` WITH `the Director has received our articles of amalgamation` IS FALSE)

-- Case: the certificate of amalgamation shows 1 May 2026. On 1 May the effects have begun; on 30 April they have not.
#ASSERT `Has the amalgamation taken effect on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the amalgamation taken effect on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30)
#ASSERT `Does the property of each amalgamating corporation now belong to the amalgamated corporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 2
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the property of each amalgamating corporation now belong to the amalgamated corporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30)
#ASSERT `Is the amalgamated corporation liable for the obligations of the corporation I dealt with` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the amalgamated corporation liable for the obligations of the corporation I dealt with` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30)
#ASSERT `Is my existing claim or liability unaffected by the amalgamation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my existing claim or liability unaffected by the amalgamation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30)
#ASSERT `Can a proceeding against the corporation I dealt with be continued against the amalgamated corporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a proceeding against the corporation I dealt with be continued against the amalgamated corporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30)
#ASSERT `Can a judgment I hold against an amalgamating corporation be enforced against the amalgamated corporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a judgment I hold against an amalgamating corporation be enforced against the amalgamated corporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30)
#ASSERT `Are the articles of amalgamation now treated as the amalgamated corporation's articles of incorporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the articles of amalgamation now treated as the amalgamated corporation's articles of incorporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30)

-- Case: an insurance company amalgamates with the corporation under the Insurance Companies Act.
#ASSERT (`May my corporation amalgamate under one of the other federal Acts` WITH `the amalgamation is under one of those other Acts` IS TRUE, `the shareholders first authorized it in accordance with section 183` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`May my corporation amalgamate under one of the other federal Acts` WITH `the amalgamation is under one of those other Acts` IS TRUE, `the shareholders first authorized it in accordance with section 183` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Outside the encoding: an ordinary CBCA amalgamation is not what s 186.1(1) is about.
#ASSERT (`May my corporation amalgamate under one of the other federal Acts` WITH `the amalgamation is under one of those other Acts` IS FALSE, `the shareholders first authorized it in accordance with section 183` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`May my corporation make a short-form amalgamation under one of the other federal Acts` WITH `the amalgamation is a short-form one under one of those other Acts` IS TRUE, `the directors first authorized it in accordance with section 184` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`May my corporation make a short-form amalgamation under one of the other federal Acts` WITH `the amalgamation is a short-form one under one of those other Acts` IS FALSE, `the directors first authorized it in accordance with section 184` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must the Director file our notice and give us a certificate of discontinuance` WITH `the Director has received our notice that we have amalgamated under another federal Act` IS TRUE, `the notice is satisfactory to the Director` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director file our notice and give us a certificate of discontinuance` WITH `the Director has received our notice that we have amalgamated under another federal Act` IS TRUE, `the notice is satisfactory to the Director` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is our notice treated as articles in the form the Director fixes` WITH `the document is the notice of an amalgamation under another federal Act` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Canada Business Corporations Act still apply to my corporation on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 31
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the Canada Business Corporations Act still apply to my corporation on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `Is my corporation freed from the articles-of-amalgamation duty of section 185 when we amalgamate under another federal Act` WITH `we amalgamate under one of those other Acts` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation freed from the articles-of-amalgamation duty of section 185 when we amalgamate under another federal Act` WITH `we amalgamate under one of those other Acts` IS FALSE)


§§ `Moving a corporation in or out: continuance (Part XV, ss 187 and 188)`

-- Case: Maple Hill Ltd., incorporated under an Ontario statute, wants to come under the CBCA.
#ASSERT `May our body corporate apply to be continued under the Canada Business Corporations Act` WITH `we were incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament` IS TRUE, `our home law authorizes us to apply` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May our body corporate apply to be continued under the Canada Business Corporations Act` WITH `we were incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament` IS FALSE, `our home law authorizes us to apply` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May our body corporate apply to be continued under the Canada Business Corporations Act` WITH `we were incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament` IS TRUE, `our home law authorizes us to apply` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can our articles of continuance make an amendment without stating it` WITH `we are applying for continuance under section 187(1)` IS TRUE, `a corporation under this Act may make that amendment to its articles` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can our articles of continuance make an amendment without stating it` WITH `we are applying for continuance under section 187(1)` IS TRUE, `a corporation under this Act may make that amendment to its articles` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Have we sent our articles of continuance to the Director as the Act requires` WITH `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS TRUE, `the documents under sections 19 and 106 went with them` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have we sent our articles of continuance to the Director as the Act requires` WITH `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS TRUE, `the documents under sections 19 and 106 went with them` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the Director give us a certificate of continuance` WITH `the Director has received our articles of continuance` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director give us a certificate of continuance` WITH `the Director has received our articles of continuance` IS FALSE)

-- Case: the certificate shows 15 June 2026.
#ASSERT `Are we a corporation under the Canada Business Corporations Act on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 15, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 15
#ASSERT NOT (`Are we a corporation under the Canada Business Corporations Act on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 15, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 14)
#ASSERT `Are our articles of continuance now our articles of incorporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 15, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 20
#ASSERT NOT (`Are our articles of continuance now our articles of incorporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 15, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 14)
#ASSERT `Is our certificate of continuance now our certificate of incorporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 15, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 15
#ASSERT NOT (`Is our certificate of continuance now our certificate of incorporation` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 15, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 14)
#ASSERT `Will the Director tell the authorities of our home jurisdiction about our continuance` WITH `the Director has issued our certificate of continuance` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the Director tell the authorities of our home jurisdiction about our continuance` WITH `the Director has issued our certificate of continuance` IS FALSE)

-- Case: after continuance (s 187(7)); before it, none of these holds.
#ASSERT `After continuance, does our property stay ours` WITH `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`After continuance, does our property stay ours` WITH `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `After continuance, are we still liable for the obligations we had before` WITH `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`After continuance, are we still liable for the obligations we had before` WITH `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `After continuance, is an existing claim or liability to prosecution unaffected` WITH `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`After continuance, is an existing claim or liability to prosecution unaffected` WITH `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `After continuance, can a pending proceeding be carried on by or against the corporation` WITH `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`After continuance, can a pending proceeding be carried on by or against the corporation` WITH `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `After continuance, can a judgment or order be enforced by or against the corporation` WITH `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`After continuance, can a judgment or order be enforced by or against the corporation` WITH `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS FALSE)

-- Case: Omar's share was issued before the continuance and was not fully paid.
#ASSERT (`Is my share, issued before our continuance, treated as validly issued under this Act` WITH `my share was issued before our body corporate was continued under this Act` IS TRUE, `section 49(8) applies to my share` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Is my share, issued before our continuance, treated as validly issued under this Act` WITH `my share was issued before our body corporate was continued under this Act` IS TRUE, `section 49(8) applies to my share` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A share issued after the continuance is outside s 187(8): the Act does not say.
#ASSERT (`Is my share, issued before our continuance, treated as validly issued under this Act` WITH `my share was issued before our body corporate was continued under this Act` IS FALSE, `section 49(8) applies to my share` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Do I keep my rights, and my liabilities, in respect of my share after our continuance` WITH `my share was issued before our body corporate was continued under this Act` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Do I keep my rights, and my liabilities, in respect of my share after our continuance` WITH `my share was issued before our body corporate was continued under this Act` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case: a holder wants to swap a registered certificate for a bearer certificate: not allowed.
#ASSERT NOT (`May we issue a bearer share certificate when a holder converts a registered one` WITH `the certificate was issued in registered form before continuance and is convertible to bearer form` IS TRUE, `the holder exercises the conversion privilege` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `May we issue a bearer share certificate when a holder converts a registered one` WITH `the certificate was issued in registered form before continuance and is convertible to bearer form` IS TRUE, `the holder exercises the conversion privilege` IS FALSE

-- Case: a share warrant is a share for these rules; some other instrument (a debenture) is not.
#ASSERT `Does my instrument count as a "share" for the continuance rules about issued shares and bearer certificates` WITH `the kind of instrument` IS `a share warrant as defined in the Canada Corporations Act`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my instrument count as a "share" for the continuance rules about issued shares and bearer certificates` WITH `the kind of instrument` IS `an instrument that is none of these`)

-- Case: par value shares.
#ASSERT `May the Director let us go on calling our shares par value shares` WITH `we applied to the Director` IS TRUE, `the Director has determined that changing the reference is not practicable` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Director let us go on calling our shares par value shares` WITH `we applied to the Director` IS TRUE, `the Director has determined that changing the reference is not practicable` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Do our articles say what they must about the largest number of par value shares` WITH `we have been permitted to go on referring to par value shares` IS TRUE, `the articles set out the maximum number of those shares` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Do our articles say what they must about the largest number of par value shares` WITH `we have been permitted to go on referring to par value shares` IS TRUE, `the articles set out the maximum number of those shares` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May we amend our articles in this way, given our par value shares` WITH `we have been permitted to go on referring to par value shares` IS TRUE, `the amendment raises the maximum number of those shares` IS TRUE, `the amendment changes the par value of those shares` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May we amend our articles in this way, given our par value shares` WITH `we have been permitted to go on referring to par value shares` IS TRUE, `the amendment raises the maximum number of those shares` IS FALSE, `the amendment changes the par value of those shares` IS FALSE

-- Case (export): the new home's laws keep everything in place except enforcement of judgments.
#ASSERT `May our corporation be continued under the laws of another jurisdiction` WITH `those laws keep our property as the new body corporate's` IS TRUE, `those laws keep the new body corporate liable for our obligations` IS TRUE, `those laws leave existing claims unaffected` IS TRUE, `those laws let pending proceedings go on` IS TRUE, `those laws let judgments be enforced` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May our corporation be continued under the laws of another jurisdiction` WITH `those laws keep our property as the new body corporate's` IS TRUE, `those laws keep the new body corporate liable for our obligations` IS TRUE, `those laws leave existing claims unaffected` IS TRUE, `those laws let pending proceedings go on` IS TRUE, `those laws let judgments be enforced` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May our corporation ask another jurisdiction to continue it there` WITH `the shareholders authorized the application` IS TRUE, `we have satisfied the Director that creditors and shareholders will not be adversely affected` IS TRUE, `the other jurisdiction's laws satisfy section 188(10)` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May our corporation ask another jurisdiction to continue it there` WITH `the shareholders authorized the application` IS TRUE, `we have satisfied the Director that creditors and shareholders will not be adversely affected` IS FALSE, `the other jurisdiction's laws satisfy section 188(10)` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `May our corporation ask a Minister to continue it under one of the other federal Acts` WITH `the shareholders authorized the application` IS TRUE, `the application is under one of those other Acts` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May our corporation ask a Minister to continue it under one of the other federal Acts` WITH `the shareholders authorized the application` IS FALSE, `the application is under one of those other Acts` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Does the notice of the continuance meeting say what the Act requires` WITH `the notice complies with section 135` IS TRUE, `the notice goes to every shareholder` IS TRUE, `shareholders have the right to dissent` IS TRUE, `the notice states that right` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the notice of the continuance meeting say what the Act requires` WITH `the notice complies with section 135` IS TRUE, `the notice goes to every shareholder` IS TRUE, `shareholders have the right to dissent` IS TRUE, `the notice states that right` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT (`Is our departure invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` WITH `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the omission does not make the action invalid`
#ASSERT (`Is our departure invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` WITH `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the Act does not say whether the omission makes the action invalid`
#ASSERT `Can I vote on the continuance elsewhere although my shares carry no other vote` WITH `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS FALSE
-- Case: 4,000 in favour, 2,000 against: exactly two-thirds. 3,999 / 2,001 is not.
#ASSERT `Have the shareholders authorized the application for continuance` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 4000, `votes cast against` IS 2000, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have the shareholders authorized the application for continuance` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 3999, `votes cast against` IS 2001, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the directors drop the application without asking the shareholders again` WITH `the shareholders authorized abandonment when they approved the application` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors drop the application without asking the shareholders again` WITH `the shareholders authorized abandonment when they approved the application` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the Director file our notice of continuance elsewhere and give us a certificate of discontinuance` WITH `the Director has received our notice of continuance elsewhere` IS TRUE, `the notice is satisfactory to the Director` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director file our notice of continuance elsewhere and give us a certificate of discontinuance` WITH `the Director has received our notice of continuance elsewhere` IS TRUE, `the notice is satisfactory to the Director` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is our notice of continuance elsewhere treated as articles in the form the Director fixes` WITH `the document is the notice referred to in section 188(7)` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Canada Business Corporations Act still govern us on the day I am asking about, after we left` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the Canada Business Corporations Act still govern us on the day I am asking about, after we left` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)


§§ `Borrowing, and selling the whole business (Part XV, s 189)`

-- Case: the directors of Oakridge Foods Inc. want to borrow from the bank; nothing in the articles, by-laws
-- or any unanimous shareholder agreement says otherwise.
#ASSERT `May the directors do this without asking the shareholders` WITH `the power` IS `to borrow money on the credit of the corporation (s 189(1)(a))`, `the articles otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides` IS FALSE
-- The by-laws require shareholder approval for borrowing: the directors cannot do it alone.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors do this without asking the shareholders` WITH `the power` IS `to borrow money on the credit of the corporation (s 189(1)(a))`, `the articles otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS TRUE, `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides` IS FALSE)
-- Giving a guarantee is a listed power; selling the corporation's shares is not.
#ASSERT `May the directors do this without asking the shareholders` WITH `the power` IS `to give a guarantee on behalf of the corporation to secure performance of an obligation of any person (s 189(1)(c))`, `the articles otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors do this without asking the shareholders` WITH `the power` IS `a power that s 189(1) does not list`, `the articles otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides` IS FALSE)

-- Case: the directors hand the borrowing powers to the chief financial officer by resolution.
#ASSERT `May the directors hand their borrowing powers to someone else` WITH `the person who would receive them` IS `an officer delegated the borrowing powers (s 189(2))`, `the directors delegate by resolution` IS TRUE, `the articles otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides` IS FALSE
-- A unanimous shareholder agreement forbids delegation.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors hand their borrowing powers to someone else` WITH `the person who would receive them` IS `an officer delegated the borrowing powers (s 189(2))`, `the directors delegate by resolution` IS TRUE, `the articles otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors hand their borrowing powers to someone else` WITH `the person who would receive them` IS `a person who is neither a director, a committee of directors nor an officer (s 189(2))`, `the directors delegate by resolution` IS TRUE, `the articles otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS FALSE, `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides` IS FALSE)

-- Case: selling the whole business.
#ASSERT `Do the shareholders have to approve this sale, lease or exchange` WITH `it is of all or substantially all the corporation's property` IS TRUE, `it is outside the ordinary course of business` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the shareholders have to approve this sale, lease or exchange` WITH `it is of all or substantially all the corporation's property` IS FALSE, `it is outside the ordinary course of business` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the shareholders have to approve this sale, lease or exchange` WITH `it is of all or substantially all the corporation's property` IS TRUE, `it is outside the ordinary course of business` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the notice of the meeting on the sale say what the Act requires` WITH `the notice complies with section 135` IS TRUE, `the notice goes to every shareholder` IS TRUE, `a copy or summary of the agreement is with the notice` IS TRUE, `shareholders have the right to dissent` IS TRUE, `the notice states that right` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the notice of the meeting on the sale say what the Act requires` WITH `the notice complies with section 135` IS TRUE, `the notice goes to every shareholder` IS TRUE, `a copy or summary of the agreement is with the notice` IS FALSE, `shareholders have the right to dissent` IS TRUE, `the notice states that right` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT (`Is the sale invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` WITH `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the omission does not make the action invalid`
#ASSERT (`Is the sale invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` WITH `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the Act does not say whether the omission makes the action invalid`
#ASSERT `May the shareholders authorize the sale and fix, or leave to the directors, its terms` WITH `this is the meeting the notice under section 189(4) called` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the shareholders authorize the sale and fix, or leave to the directors, its terms` WITH `this is the meeting the notice under section 189(4) called` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can I vote on the sale although my shares carry no other vote` WITH `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS FALSE
-- Class vote only if the class is affected differently.
#ASSERT `Does my class or series vote separately on the sale` WITH `my class or series is affected in a manner different from the shares of another class or series` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my class or series vote separately on the sale` WITH `my class or series is affected in a manner different from the shares of another class or series` IS FALSE)
-- Adopted: 2,000 / 1,000 is exactly two-thirds; 1,999 / 1,001 is not; a failed class vote defeats it.
#ASSERT `Have the shareholders adopted the sale, lease or exchange` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 2000, `votes cast against` IS 1000, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE, `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have the shareholders adopted the sale, lease or exchange` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 1999, `votes cast against` IS 1001, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE, `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Have the shareholders adopted the sale, lease or exchange` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 2000, `votes cast against` IS 1000, `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS FALSE, `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS FALSE)
-- The approving resolution authorized the directors to walk away, and no third party's right would be defeated.
#ASSERT `May the directors drop an approved sale without asking the shareholders again` WITH `the shareholders authorized abandonment when they approved the sale` IS TRUE, `abandoning it would defeat a right of a third party` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors drop an approved sale without asking the shareholders again` WITH `the shareholders authorized abandonment when they approved the sale` IS TRUE, `abandoning it would defeat a right of a third party` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors drop an approved sale without asking the shareholders again` WITH `the shareholders authorized abandonment when they approved the sale` IS FALSE, `abandoning it would defeat a right of a third party` IS FALSE)


§§ `Dissenting: asking the corporation to buy my shares (Part XV, s 190)`

-- Case: Dana holds 1,000 Class B shares of Elmwood Corp. On 1 March 2026 Elmwood's shareholders resolve to
-- amalgamate under section 183 (not the short form of section 184). Dana objects in writing before the
-- meeting. She may dissent (s 190(1)(c)).
#ASSERT `May I dissent from what my corporation is doing` WITH `what the corporation is doing` IS `a resolution to amalgamate otherwise than under section 184 (s 190(1)(c))`, `the provisions concern my class of shares` IS FALSE, `the amendment is made under section 191 (court-ordered reorganization)` IS FALSE, `section 241 displaces the right to dissent` IS FALSE
-- A short-form amalgamation under section 184 is not on the list: no right.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I dissent from what my corporation is doing` WITH `what the corporation is doing` IS `an action that s 190(1) does not list`, `the provisions concern my class of shares` IS FALSE, `the amendment is made under section 191 (court-ordered reorganization)` IS FALSE, `section 241 displaces the right to dissent` IS FALSE)
-- An amendment limiting ownership of a different class: not Dana's class.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I dissent from what my corporation is doing` WITH `what the corporation is doing` IS `a resolution to amend the articles under section 173 or 174 to add, change or remove provisions restricting or constraining the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of that class (s 190(1)(a))`, `the provisions concern my class of shares` IS FALSE, `the amendment is made under section 191 (court-ordered reorganization)` IS FALSE, `section 241 displaces the right to dissent` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May I dissent from what my corporation is doing` WITH `what the corporation is doing` IS `a resolution to amend the articles under section 173 or 174 to add, change or remove provisions restricting or constraining the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of that class (s 190(1)(a))`, `the provisions concern my class of shares` IS TRUE, `the amendment is made under section 191 (court-ordered reorganization)` IS FALSE, `section 241 displaces the right to dissent` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I dissent from what my corporation is doing` WITH `what the corporation is doing` IS `a resolution to be continued under section 188 (s 190(1)(d))`, `the provisions concern my class of shares` IS FALSE, `the amendment is made under section 191 (court-ordered reorganization)` IS TRUE, `section 241 displaces the right to dissent` IS FALSE)

-- Case: the amendment changes the rights of Dana's class, so her class votes separately; she may dissent.
#ASSERT `May I dissent from an amendment because my class or series has a separate vote on it` WITH `what the amendment does to my class` IS `a change to the rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached to the shares of the class (s 176(1)(c))`, `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS FALSE, `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS FALSE, `the amendment only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS FALSE, `my shares are a series of a class` IS FALSE, `my series is affected differently` IS FALSE, `the corporation has resolved to amend its articles in that way` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I dissent from an amendment because my class or series has a separate vote on it` WITH `what the amendment does to my class` IS `no effect that s 176(1) lists`, `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS FALSE, `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS FALSE, `the amendment only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS FALSE, `my shares are a series of a class` IS FALSE, `my series is affected differently` IS FALSE, `the corporation has resolved to amend its articles in that way` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May I dissent from an amendment because my class or series has a separate vote on it` WITH `what the amendment does to my class` IS `a change to the rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached to the shares of the class (s 176(1)(c))`, `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS FALSE, `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS FALSE, `the amendment only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS FALSE, `my shares are a series of a class` IS FALSE, `my series is affected differently` IS FALSE, `the corporation has resolved to amend its articles in that way` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can I dissent even though my corporation has only one class of shares` WITH `my corporation has only one class of shares` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I dissent even though my corporation has only one class of shares` WITH `my corporation has only one class of shares` IS FALSE

-- Case: Dana took every step; the amalgamation took effect.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be paid the fair value of my shares` WITH `my claim covers all the shares as subsection 190(4) requires` IS TRUE, `I met the objection requirement` IS TRUE, `my demand for payment was in time and complete` IS TRUE, `my certificates were sent in time` IS TRUE, `the action or order has become effective` IS TRUE
-- Her certificates were late: she did not comply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to be paid the fair value of my shares` WITH `my claim covers all the shares as subsection 190(4) requires` IS TRUE, `I met the objection requirement` IS TRUE, `my demand for payment was in time and complete` IS TRUE, `my certificates were sent in time` IS FALSE, `the action or order has become effective` IS TRUE)
-- Not yet effective: not yet entitled.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to be paid the fair value of my shares` WITH `my claim covers all the shares as subsection 190(4) requires` IS TRUE, `I met the objection requirement` IS TRUE, `my demand for payment was in time and complete` IS TRUE, `my certificates were sent in time` IS TRUE, `the action or order has become effective` IS FALSE)
-- The resolution was adopted on 1 March 2026: fair value is fixed as of 28 February.
#ASSERT (`As of what day is the fair value of my shares determined` WITH `the day the resolution was adopted or the order was made` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 28
-- Dana holds 1,000 Class B shares for one beneficial owner; she claims all 1,000. A claim for 600 would not do.
#ASSERT `Does my claim cover the right number of shares` WITH `the number of shares of the class that my claim covers` IS 1000, `the number of shares of the class held for that beneficial owner and registered in my name` IS 1000
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my claim cover the right number of shares` WITH `the number of shares of the class that my claim covers` IS 600, `the number of shares of the class held for that beneficial owner and registered in my name` IS 1000)

-- Case: objection.
#ASSERT `Have I met the requirement to object in writing` WITH `I sent the corporation a written objection at or before the meeting` IS TRUE, `the corporation gave me no notice of the meeting's purpose and my right to dissent` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I met the requirement to object in writing` WITH `I sent the corporation a written objection at or before the meeting` IS FALSE, `the corporation gave me no notice of the meeting's purpose and my right to dissent` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I met the requirement to object in writing` WITH `I sent the corporation a written objection at or before the meeting` IS FALSE, `the corporation gave me no notice of the meeting's purpose and my right to dissent` IS FALSE)

-- Case: notice that the resolution was adopted (1 March 2026): Dana objected, did not vote for it and did
-- not withdraw, so Elmwood must send her notice by 11 March.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation send me notice that the resolution has been adopted` WITH `I filed an objection` IS TRUE, `I voted for the resolution` IS FALSE, `I withdrew my objection` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the corporation send me notice that the resolution has been adopted` WITH `I filed an objection` IS TRUE, `I voted for the resolution` IS TRUE, `I withdrew my objection` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT (`By what day must the corporation send me notice that the resolution was adopted` WITH `the day the shareholders adopted the resolution` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 11
#ASSERT `Did the corporation send me notice that the resolution was adopted in time` WITH `the day the shareholders adopted the resolution` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the day the corporation sent the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 11
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the corporation send me notice that the resolution was adopted in time` WITH `the day the shareholders adopted the resolution` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the day the corporation sent the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 12)

-- Case: Dana received the notice on 12 March: her demand is due by 1 April. Another shareholder, Ravi,
-- got no notice and learned of the adoption on 5 March: his demand is due by 25 March.
#ASSERT (`By what day must I send my demand for payment` WITH `I received a notice under subsection 190(6)` IS TRUE, `the day I received that notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 12, `the day I learned that the resolution had been adopted` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1
#ASSERT (`By what day must I send my demand for payment` WITH `I received a notice under subsection 190(6)` IS FALSE, `the day I received that notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 12, `the day I learned that the resolution had been adopted` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 25
#ASSERT `Did I send my demand for payment in time` WITH `I received a notice under subsection 190(6)` IS TRUE, `the day I received that notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 12, `the day I learned that the resolution had been adopted` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 5, `the day I sent my demand` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I send my demand for payment in time` WITH `I received a notice under subsection 190(6)` IS TRUE, `the day I received that notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 12, `the day I learned that the resolution had been adopted` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 5, `the day I sent my demand` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 2)
#ASSERT `Does my demand for payment say everything the Act requires` WITH `it contains my name and address` IS TRUE, `it contains the number and class of my shares` IS TRUE, `it demands payment of the fair value` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my demand for payment say everything the Act requires` WITH `it contains my name and address` IS TRUE, `it contains the number and class of my shares` IS FALSE, `it demands payment of the fair value` IS TRUE)

-- Case: Dana sent her demand on 1 April: certificates due by 1 May.
#ASSERT (`By what day must I send in my share certificates` WITH `the day I sent my demand for payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1
#ASSERT `Did I send in my share certificates in time` WITH `the day I sent my demand for payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1, `the day I sent my certificates` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I send in my share certificates in time` WITH `the day I sent my demand for payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1, `the day I sent my certificates` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 2)
#ASSERT `Do I lose my claim because I did not send my certificates properly` WITH `I complied with subsection 190(8)` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I lose my claim because I did not send my certificates properly` WITH `I complied with subsection 190(8)` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Must the corporation endorse my certificate and give it back to me` WITH `the corporation or its transfer agent received my certificate` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the corporation endorse my certificate and give it back to me` WITH `the corporation or its transfer agent received my certificate` IS FALSE)

-- Case: suspension of rights after the demand; restored if she withdraws before an offer.
#ASSERT `Am I left with only the right to be paid for my shares` WITH `I have sent a demand for payment` IS TRUE, `I withdrew it before the corporation made an offer` IS FALSE, `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with section 190(12)` IS FALSE, `I withdrew it` IS FALSE, `the directors called the action off` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I left with only the right to be paid for my shares` WITH `I have sent a demand for payment` IS TRUE, `I withdrew it before the corporation made an offer` IS TRUE, `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with section 190(12)` IS FALSE, `I withdrew it` IS TRUE, `the directors called the action off` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Have my rights as a shareholder been restored` WITH `I have sent a demand for payment` IS TRUE, `I withdrew it before the corporation made an offer` IS FALSE, `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with section 190(12)` IS FALSE, `I withdrew it` IS FALSE, `the directors called the action off` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have my rights as a shareholder been restored` WITH `I have sent a demand for payment` IS TRUE, `I withdrew it before the corporation made an offer` IS FALSE, `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with section 190(12)` IS TRUE, `I withdrew it` IS FALSE, `the directors called the action off` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT (`From what day do my restored rights count` WITH `the day I sent my demand for payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1, `my rights have been restored` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT (`From what day do my restored rights count` WITH `the day I sent my demand for payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1, `my rights have been restored` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case: the amalgamation takes effect 10 April; Elmwood received Dana's demand 4 April: seven days from the
-- later day, 10 April: offer due by 17 April.
#ASSERT (`By what day must the corporation make me an offer` WITH `the day the action became effective` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 10, `the day the corporation received my demand for payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 4) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 17
#ASSERT `Did the corporation make me an offer in time` WITH `the day the action became effective` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 10, `the day the corporation received my demand for payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 4, `the day the corporation sent its offer or notification` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 17
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the corporation make me an offer in time` WITH `the day the action became effective` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 10, `the day the corporation received my demand for payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 4, `the day the corporation sent its offer or notification` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 18)
#ASSERT `Did the corporation respond to my demand as the Act requires` WITH `the corporation sent a written offer to pay` IS TRUE, `the offer is for what the directors consider the fair value` IS TRUE, `the offer has a statement of how the fair value was determined` IS TRUE, `the corporation says it may not lawfully pay` IS FALSE, `the corporation sent a notification that it is unable to pay lawfully` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the corporation respond to my demand as the Act requires` WITH `the corporation sent a written offer to pay` IS TRUE, `the offer is for what the directors consider the fair value` IS TRUE, `the offer has a statement of how the fair value was determined` IS FALSE, `the corporation says it may not lawfully pay` IS FALSE, `the corporation sent a notification that it is unable to pay lawfully` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Did the corporation respond to my demand as the Act requires` WITH `the corporation sent a written offer to pay` IS FALSE, `the offer is for what the directors consider the fair value` IS FALSE, `the offer has a statement of how the fair value was determined` IS FALSE, `the corporation says it may not lawfully pay` IS TRUE, `the corporation sent a notification that it is unable to pay lawfully` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the corporation's offers to holders of my class on the same terms` WITH `the offers are for shares of the same class or series` IS TRUE, `the offers are on the same terms` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the corporation's offers to holders of my class on the same terms` WITH `the offers are for shares of the same class or series` IS TRUE, `the offers are on the same terms` IS FALSE)
-- Dana accepts: Elmwood pays within ten days (accepted 20 April: pay by 30 April), unless it cannot lawfully.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation pay me for my shares now` WITH `I have accepted the offer` IS TRUE, `the corporation may not lawfully pay` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the corporation pay me for my shares now` WITH `I have accepted the offer` IS TRUE, `the corporation may not lawfully pay` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT (`By what day must the corporation pay me after I accept its offer` WITH `the day I accepted the offer` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 20) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30
#ASSERT `Did the corporation pay me in time` WITH `the day I accepted the offer` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 20, `the day the corporation paid me` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the corporation pay me in time` WITH `the day I accepted the offer` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 20, `the day the corporation paid me` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)
-- The offer was made 17 April: acceptance due 17 May; it lapses after that if none arrives.
#ASSERT (`By what day must the corporation receive my acceptance of its offer` WITH `the day the corporation made me the offer` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 17) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 17
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the corporation's offer lapsed on the day I am asking about` WITH `the day the corporation made me the offer` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 17, `the corporation has received an acceptance` IS FALSE, `the day the corporation received my acceptance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 17, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 17)
#ASSERT `Has the corporation's offer lapsed on the day I am asking about` WITH `the day the corporation made me the offer` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 17, `the corporation has received an acceptance` IS FALSE, `the day the corporation received my acceptance` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 17, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 18

-- Case: the court. The action took effect 1 June 2026. Elmwood makes no offer: it may apply to a court
-- until 21 July; if it does not, Dana may apply from 22 July until 10 August.
#ASSERT `May the corporation ask a court to fix the value of my shares` WITH `the corporation failed to make an offer` IS TRUE, `I failed to accept an offer` IS FALSE, `the day the action became effective` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day the corporation applied to the court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21, `a court has allowed a further period` IS FALSE, `the last day of the further period` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1
#ASSERT NOT (`May the corporation ask a court to fix the value of my shares` WITH `the corporation failed to make an offer` IS TRUE, `I failed to accept an offer` IS FALSE, `the day the action became effective` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day the corporation applied to the court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 22, `a court has allowed a further period` IS FALSE, `the last day of the further period` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT (`By what day may the corporation ask a court to fix the value` WITH `the day the action became effective` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21
#ASSERT `May I ask a court to fix the value of my shares myself` WITH `the corporation failed to apply to a court` IS TRUE, `the day the action became effective` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day I apply to the court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 10, `a court has allowed me a further period` IS FALSE, `the last day of the further period` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1
#ASSERT NOT (`May I ask a court to fix the value of my shares myself` WITH `the corporation failed to apply to a court` IS TRUE, `the day the action became effective` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day I apply to the court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 11, `a court has allowed me a further period` IS FALSE, `the last day of the further period` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT (`By what day may I ask a court to fix the value of my shares` WITH `the day the action became effective` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 8 10
#ASSERT `Is this the right court to apply to` WITH `it has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` IS TRUE, `it has jurisdiction in the province where I live` IS FALSE, `the corporation carries on business in my province` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this the right court to apply to` WITH `it has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` IS FALSE, `it has jurisdiction in the province where I live` IS TRUE, `the corporation carries on business in my province` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this the right court to apply to` WITH `it has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` IS FALSE, `it has jurisdiction in the province where I live` IS TRUE, `the corporation carries on business in my province` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT (`Must I give security for costs when I apply to the court` WITH `the application is under subsection 190(15) or 190(16)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Must I give security for costs when I apply to the court` WITH `the application is under subsection 190(15) or 190(16)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Will I be a party to the court application and bound by its decision` WITH `the corporation has not purchased my shares` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Will I be a party to the court application and bound by its decision` WITH `the corporation has not purchased my shares` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Has the corporation told me what it must about the court application` WITH `its notice states the date` IS TRUE, `its notice states the place` IS TRUE, `its notice states the consequences` IS TRUE, `its notice states my right to appear and be heard` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the corporation told me what it must about the court application` WITH `its notice states the date` IS TRUE, `its notice states the place` IS TRUE, `its notice states the consequences` IS FALSE, `its notice states my right to appear and be heard` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Will the court fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting shareholders together` WITH `an application has been made` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the court fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting shareholders together` WITH `an application has been made` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the court appoint appraisers to help fix the value` WITH `an application has been made` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Will the court's final order be against the corporation and in my favour` WITH `the court has fixed a fair value` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the court's final order be against the corporation and in my favour` WITH `the court has fixed a fair value` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the court allow interest on what I am owed for the day I am asking about` WITH `the day the action became effective` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day of payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court allow interest on what I am owed for the day I am asking about` WITH `the day the action became effective` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day of payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)

-- Case: Elmwood cannot lawfully pay (it would be unable to pay its debts as they fall due). The court
-- pronounced its order 1 August 2026: Elmwood must tell Dana by 11 August; Dana received that on 15 August
-- and has until 14 September to choose.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation refuse to pay me because it cannot lawfully do so` WITH `it is or would after the payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS TRUE, `the realizable value of its assets would thereby be less than its liabilities` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the corporation refuse to pay me because it cannot lawfully do so` WITH `it is or would after the payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS FALSE, `the realizable value of its assets would thereby be less than its liabilities` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the corporation refuse to pay me because it cannot lawfully do so` WITH `it is or would after the payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS FALSE, `the realizable value of its assets would thereby be less than its liabilities` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the corporation tell me it cannot lawfully pay` WITH `section 190(26) applies` IS TRUE, `a court has pronounced a final order` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the corporation tell me it cannot lawfully pay` WITH `section 190(26) applies` IS FALSE, `a court has pronounced a final order` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT (`By what day must the corporation tell me it cannot lawfully pay` WITH `the day the court pronounced the order` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 8 11
#ASSERT `Did the corporation tell me in time that it cannot lawfully pay` WITH `the day the court pronounced the order` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 1, `the day the corporation gave me the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 11
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the corporation tell me in time that it cannot lawfully pay` WITH `the day the court pronounced the order` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 1, `the day the corporation gave me the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 12)
#ASSERT (`By what day must I answer the corporation's notice that it cannot pay` WITH `the day I received the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 9 14
#ASSERT `Did I answer the corporation's notice that it cannot pay in time` WITH `the day I received the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 15, `the day I delivered my written notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 9 14
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I answer the corporation's notice that it cannot pay in time` WITH `the day I received the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 15, `the day I delivered my written notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 9 15)
#ASSERT (`What happens if I withdraw my dissent, or stay on as a claimant` WITH `section 190(26) applies` IS TRUE, `I delivered my written notice in time` IS TRUE, `my choice` IS `to withdraw the notice of dissent`) EQUALS `the corporation is deemed to consent to the withdrawal and the shareholder is reinstated to their full rights as a shareholder`
#ASSERT (`What happens if I withdraw my dissent, or stay on as a claimant` WITH `section 190(26) applies` IS TRUE, `I delivered my written notice in time` IS TRUE, `my choice` IS `to retain a status as a claimant against the corporation`) EQUALS `the shareholder is a claimant, paid as soon as the corporation is lawfully able to do so, or in a liquidation ranked after the creditors and before the shareholders`
-- Outside the encoding: she delivered her notice late.
#ASSERT (`What happens if I withdraw my dissent, or stay on as a claimant` WITH `section 190(26) applies` IS TRUE, `I delivered my written notice in time` IS FALSE, `my choice` IS `to withdraw the notice of dissent`) EQUALS `the Act does not say what the effect is`


§§ `Court-ordered reorganization and arrangement (Part XV, ss 191 and 192)`

-- Case: a court makes an oppression-remedy order (s 241) against Harbour Foods Inc. Wei, a shareholder.
#ASSERT `Is this court order a reorganization under the Act` WITH `the kind of order` IS `an order made under section 241`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this court order a reorganization under the Act` WITH `the kind of order` IS `an order that is none of these`)
#ASSERT `May the court's order amend our articles in this way` WITH `our corporation is subject to a reorganization order` IS TRUE, `the change is one an amendment under section 173 could lawfully make` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court's order amend our articles in this way` WITH `our corporation is subject to a reorganization order` IS TRUE, `the change is one an amendment under section 173 could lawfully make` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the court authorize our corporation to issue debt obligations and fix their terms` WITH `a court has made a reorganization order` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court authorize our corporation to issue debt obligations and fix their terms` WITH `a court has made a reorganization order` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the court replace or add to our directors` WITH `a court has made a reorganization order` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court replace or add to our directors` WITH `a court has made a reorganization order` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must we send articles of reorganization to the Director` WITH `a reorganization order has been made` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must we send articles of reorganization to the Director` WITH `a reorganization order has been made` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Have we sent our articles of reorganization to the Director as the Act requires` WITH `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS TRUE, `sections 19 and 113 call for documents` IS TRUE, `we sent those documents with them` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Have we sent our articles of reorganization to the Director as the Act requires` WITH `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS TRUE, `sections 19 and 113 call for documents` IS FALSE, `we sent those documents with them` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have we sent our articles of reorganization to the Director as the Act requires` WITH `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS TRUE, `sections 19 and 113 call for documents` IS TRUE, `we sent those documents with them` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the Director give us a certificate of amendment for our reorganization` WITH `the Director has received our articles of reorganization` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director give us a certificate of amendment for our reorganization` WITH `the Director has received our articles of reorganization` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Has our reorganization taken effect on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 9 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 9 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Has our reorganization taken effect on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 9 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 31)
-- Wei cannot dissent from an amendment made under section 191.
#ASSERT `Am I shut out of dissenting because the amendment was made by a reorganization order` WITH `the amendment to the articles was effected under section 191` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I shut out of dissenting because the amendment was made by a reorganization order` WITH `the amendment to the articles was effected under section 191` IS FALSE)

-- Case: arrangement.
#ASSERT (`Is this transaction an "arrangement" under the Act` WITH `the kind of transaction` IS `a division of the business carried on by a corporation (s 192(1)(d))`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A share buy-back by the company is not on the list: the Act does not say.
#ASSERT (`Is this transaction an "arrangement" under the Act` WITH `the kind of transaction` IS `a transaction that is not named in s 192(1)`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Assets 1,000; liabilities 600; stated capital 400: exactly balanced, so not insolvent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation insolvent under the Act` WITH `we are unable to pay our liabilities as they become due` IS FALSE, `the realizable value of our assets` IS 1000, `the aggregate of our liabilities` IS 600, `the stated capital of all our classes` IS 400)
#ASSERT `Is my corporation insolvent under the Act` WITH `we are unable to pay our liabilities as they become due` IS FALSE, `the realizable value of our assets` IS 999, `the aggregate of our liabilities` IS 600, `the stated capital of all our classes` IS 400
#ASSERT `Is my corporation insolvent under the Act` WITH `we are unable to pay our liabilities as they become due` IS TRUE, `the realizable value of our assets` IS 5000, `the aggregate of our liabilities` IS 100, `the stated capital of all our classes` IS 100
#ASSERT `May my corporation ask a court to approve an arrangement` WITH `we are unable to pay our liabilities as they become due` IS FALSE, `the realizable value of our assets` IS 1000, `the aggregate of our liabilities` IS 600, `the stated capital of all our classes` IS 400, `it is not practicable to make the change under another provision` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation ask a court to approve an arrangement` WITH `we are unable to pay our liabilities as they become due` IS TRUE, `the realizable value of our assets` IS 1000, `the aggregate of our liabilities` IS 600, `the stated capital of all our classes` IS 400, `it is not practicable to make the change under another provision` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation ask a court to approve an arrangement` WITH `we are unable to pay our liabilities as they become due` IS FALSE, `the realizable value of our assets` IS 1000, `the aggregate of our liabilities` IS 600, `the stated capital of all our classes` IS 400, `it is not practicable to make the change under another provision` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the court make this order on our application` WITH `an application has been made under section 192` IS TRUE, `the court thinks the order fit` IS TRUE, `the order` IS `an order permitting a shareholder to dissent under section 190 (s 192(4)(d))`
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court make this order on our application` WITH `an application has been made under section 192` IS TRUE, `the court thinks the order fit` IS TRUE, `the order` IS `an order dispensing with notice to the Director`)
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court make this order on our application` WITH `an application has been made under section 192` IS TRUE, `the court thinks the order fit` IS FALSE, `the order` IS `any other interim or final order the court thinks fit`)
#ASSERT `Must we give the Director notice of our application to the court` WITH `we have applied for an interim or final order under section 192` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must we give the Director notice of our application to the court` WITH `we have applied for an interim or final order under section 192` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on the application` WITH `an application for an interim or final order under section 192 has been made` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on the application` WITH `an application for an interim or final order under section 192 has been made` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must we send articles of arrangement to the Director` WITH `the court has approved the arrangement` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must we send articles of arrangement to the Director` WITH `the court has approved the arrangement` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Have we sent our articles of arrangement to the Director as the Act requires` WITH `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS TRUE, `sections 19 and 113 call for documents` IS FALSE, `we sent those documents with them` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have we sent our articles of arrangement to the Director as the Act requires` WITH `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS FALSE, `sections 19 and 113 call for documents` IS FALSE, `we sent those documents with them` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the Director give us a certificate of arrangement` WITH `the Director has received our articles of arrangement` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director give us a certificate of arrangement` WITH `the Director has received our articles of arrangement` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Has our arrangement taken effect on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of arrangement` IS YearMonthDay 2026 10 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 10 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Has our arrangement taken effect on the day I am asking about` WITH `the date shown in the certificate of arrangement` IS YearMonthDay 2026 10 1, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 9 30)


§§ `Going private and squeeze-outs (Part XVI, ss 193 and 194)`

-- Case: Birchwood Ltd., a private corporation, wants to buy out minority holders for cash, which needs an
-- amendment to its articles and ends their interest without their consent. It is a squeeze-out transaction.
#ASSERT `Is this a squeeze-out transaction` WITH `the transaction is by a corporation` IS TRUE, `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS FALSE, `the transaction would require an amendment to the corporation's articles` IS TRUE, `the transaction would terminate a holder's interest without their consent` IS TRUE, `an interest of equivalent value is substituted` IS FALSE, `the substituted interest is in shares issued by the corporation` IS FALSE, `those shares have equal or greater rights and privileges` IS FALSE
-- A distributing corporation's transaction is not one.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this a squeeze-out transaction` WITH `the transaction is by a corporation` IS TRUE, `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS TRUE, `the transaction would require an amendment to the corporation's articles` IS TRUE, `the transaction would terminate a holder's interest without their consent` IS TRUE, `an interest of equivalent value is substituted` IS FALSE, `the substituted interest is in shares issued by the corporation` IS FALSE, `those shares have equal or greater rights and privileges` IS FALSE)

#ASSERT `May my corporation carry out a going-private transaction` WITH `there are applicable provincial securities laws` IS FALSE, `our corporation complies with those laws` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `May my corporation carry out a going-private transaction` WITH `there are applicable provincial securities laws` IS TRUE, `our corporation complies with those laws` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation carry out a going-private transaction` WITH `there are applicable provincial securities laws` IS TRUE, `our corporation complies with those laws` IS FALSE)

-- Case: Priya holds Class C shares which carry no vote, and the parent (an affiliate) wants the shares.
#ASSERT `May I vote on the squeeze-out resolution` WITH `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS FALSE, `I am an affiliate of the corporation` IS FALSE, `I would get greater value or superior rights than other holders of my class` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I vote on the squeeze-out resolution` WITH `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS TRUE, `I am an affiliate of the corporation` IS TRUE, `I would get greater value or superior rights than other holders of my class` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May I vote on the squeeze-out resolution` WITH `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS TRUE, `I am an affiliate of the corporation` IS FALSE, `I would get greater value or superior rights than other holders of my class` IS TRUE)
-- Priya's class (eligible holders) voted 51 to 49: a majority; 50 to 50 is not.
#ASSERT `Has my class approved the squeeze-out transaction by ordinary resolution` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 51, `votes cast against` IS 49
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my class approved the squeeze-out transaction by ordinary resolution` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS 50, `votes cast against` IS 50)
#ASSERT (`May my corporation carry out this squeeze-out transaction` WITH `it is a squeeze-out transaction` IS TRUE, `the other approvals have been obtained` IS TRUE, `every affected class approved it by ordinary resolution` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`May my corporation carry out this squeeze-out transaction` WITH `it is a squeeze-out transaction` IS TRUE, `the other approvals have been obtained` IS TRUE, `every affected class approved it by ordinary resolution` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A transaction that is not a squeeze-out transaction: s 194 sets no condition.
#ASSERT (`May my corporation carry out this squeeze-out transaction` WITH `it is a squeeze-out transaction` IS FALSE, `the other approvals have been obtained` IS FALSE, `every affected class approved it by ordinary resolution` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING


§§ `Take-over bids: being bought out, or buying out (Part XVII, ss 206 and 206.1)`

-- Case: Quill Ltd., a distributing corporation, receives a take-over bid dated 1 March 2026 from Rivet Inc.
-- for all its common shares. Maya holds common shares and has not accepted the bid: she is a dissenting offeree.
#ASSERT `Am I a dissenting offeree` WITH `a take-over bid was made for all the shares of my class` IS TRUE, `I hold a share of that class` IS TRUE, `I have accepted the take-over bid` IS FALSE, `I acquired my share from a holder who had not accepted` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a dissenting offeree` WITH `a take-over bid was made for all the shares of my class` IS TRUE, `I hold a share of that class` IS TRUE, `I have accepted the take-over bid` IS TRUE, `I acquired my share from a holder who had not accepted` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I a dissenting offeree` WITH `a take-over bid was made for all the shares of my class` IS TRUE, `I hold a share of that class` IS FALSE, `I have accepted the take-over bid` IS FALSE, `I acquired my share from a holder who had not accepted` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this offer a take-over bid under the Act` WITH `it is made by an offeror to shareholders of a distributing corporation` IS TRUE, `it is made at about the same time to all of them` IS TRUE, `it is to acquire all the shares of a class of issued shares` IS TRUE, `it is a distributing corporation's offer to repurchase all the shares of a class` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this offer a take-over bid under the Act` WITH `it is made by an offeror to shareholders of a distributing corporation` IS TRUE, `it is made at about the same time to all of them` IS TRUE, `it is to acquire all the shares of a class of issued shares` IS FALSE, `it is a distributing corporation's offer to repurchase all the shares of a class` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is this offer a take-over bid under the Act` WITH `it is made by an offeror to shareholders of a distributing corporation` IS FALSE, `it is made at about the same time to all of them` IS FALSE, `it is to acquire all the shares of a class of issued shares` IS FALSE, `it is a distributing corporation's offer to repurchase all the shares of a class` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my interest count as a "share" in the take-over rules` WITH `the kind of interest` IS `a currently exercisable option or right to acquire such a share or such a convertible security (s 206(1) share (b))`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my interest count as a "share" in the take-over rules` WITH `the kind of interest` IS `an interest that is none of these`)
#ASSERT `Is this person an offeror` WITH `the person makes a take-over bid` IS TRUE, `the person is only an agent or mandatary` IS FALSE, `the person makes bids jointly or in concert with others` IS FALSE, `the person intends to vote jointly or in concert with others` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this person an offeror` WITH `the person makes a take-over bid` IS TRUE, `the person is only an agent or mandatary` IS TRUE, `the person makes bids jointly or in concert with others` IS FALSE, `the person intends to vote jointly or in concert with others` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is this person an offeror` WITH `the person makes a take-over bid` IS FALSE, `the person is only an agent or mandatary` IS FALSE, `the person makes bids jointly or in concert with others` IS FALSE, `the person intends to vote jointly or in concert with others` IS TRUE

-- Case: Quill has 1,000 shares of the class; Rivet and its affiliates hold 100 of them. 810 acceptances arrive
-- in time (90 per cent of the 900 others): Rivet is entitled to buy out the holdouts, if it complies.
#ASSERT `Is the offeror entitled to buy out the holdouts` WITH `the number of shares of the class to which the bid relates` IS 1000, `the number held by the offeror or its affiliates or associates` IS 100, `the number accepted within 120 days` IS 810, `the offeror complies with section 206` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the offeror entitled to buy out the holdouts` WITH `the number of shares of the class to which the bid relates` IS 1000, `the number held by the offeror or its affiliates or associates` IS 100, `the number accepted within 120 days` IS 809, `the offeror complies with section 206` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the offeror entitled to buy out the holdouts` WITH `the number of shares of the class to which the bid relates` IS 1000, `the number held by the offeror or its affiliates or associates` IS 100, `the number accepted within 120 days` IS 810, `the offeror complies with section 206` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT (`By what day must an acceptance be received to count toward the 90 per cent` WITH `the date of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 29
#ASSERT `Does an acceptance received on a given day count toward the 90 per cent` WITH `the date of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the day the acceptance was received` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 29
#ASSERT NOT (`Does an acceptance received on a given day count toward the 90 per cent` WITH `the date of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the day the acceptance was received` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)

-- Case: the bid ended 1 June 2026: notice is due by 31 July (60 days after termination), earlier than
-- 28 August (180 days after the bid).
#ASSERT (`By what day must the offeror send me its notice` WITH `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the date of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 7 31
#ASSERT `Did the offeror send me its notice in time` WITH `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the date of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the day the offeror sent the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 31
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the offeror send me its notice in time` WITH `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the date of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the day the offeror sent the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 1)
#ASSERT `Does the offeror's notice say everything the Act requires` WITH `it says that holders of at least 90 per cent accepted` IS TRUE, `it says the offeror is bound to take up and pay for the shares` IS TRUE, `it says I must elect to transfer or demand fair value within 20 days` IS TRUE, `it says that silence is a deemed election to transfer` IS TRUE, `it says I must send my shares within 20 days` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the offeror's notice say everything the Act requires` WITH `it says that holders of at least 90 per cent accepted` IS TRUE, `it says the offeror is bound to take up and pay for the shares` IS TRUE, `it says I must elect to transfer or demand fair value within 20 days` IS TRUE, `it says that silence is a deemed election to transfer` IS FALSE, `it says I must send my shares within 20 days` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Was the offeror's notice sent in the way the Act requires` WITH `it was sent by registered mail` IS TRUE, `it was sent to every dissenting offeree` IS TRUE, `it was sent to the Director` IS TRUE, `it was sent in time` IS TRUE, `it says what section 206(3) requires` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the offeror's notice sent in the way the Act requires` WITH `it was sent by registered mail` IS FALSE, `it was sent to every dissenting offeree` IS TRUE, `it was sent to the Director` IS TRUE, `it was sent in time` IS TRUE, `it says what section 206(3) requires` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Must the offeror send the offeree corporation a notice of adverse claim about my shares` WITH `the offeror sends an offeror's notice to dissenting offerees` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the offeror send the offeree corporation a notice of adverse claim about my shares` WITH `the offeror sends an offeror's notice to dissenting offerees` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is the offeror's notice of adverse claim in order` WITH `it was sent at the same time as the offeror's notice` IS TRUE, `it follows section 78` IS TRUE, `it covers each share a dissenting offeree holds` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the offeror's notice of adverse claim in order` WITH `it was sent at the same time as the offeror's notice` IS TRUE, `it follows section 78` IS TRUE, `it covers each share a dissenting offeree holds` IS FALSE)

-- Case: Maya received the notice on 1 July 2026: she must send her certificates and elect by 21 July.
#ASSERT (`By what day must I send my share certificates and make my election` WITH `the day I received the offeror's notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21
#ASSERT `Did I send my share certificates in time` WITH `the day I received the offeror's notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day I sent my certificates` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I send my share certificates in time` WITH `the day I received the offeror's notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day I sent my certificates` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 22)
#ASSERT (`Am I treated as having taken the bid's terms, or as demanding fair value` WITH `I notified the offeror that I demand fair value` IS TRUE, `the day I received the offeror's notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day I notified the offeror` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21) EQUALS `to demand payment of the fair value of the shares`
-- If she says nothing, or too late, she is deemed to have elected to transfer.
#ASSERT (`Am I treated as having taken the bid's terms, or as demanding fair value` WITH `I notified the offeror that I demand fair value` IS TRUE, `the day I received the offeror's notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day I notified the offeror` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 22) EQUALS `to transfer the shares on the terms on which the offeror acquired the shares of the offerees who accepted`
#ASSERT (`Am I treated as having taken the bid's terms, or as demanding fair value` WITH `I notified the offeror that I demand fair value` IS FALSE, `the day I received the offeror's notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day I notified the offeror` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS `to transfer the shares on the terms on which the offeror acquired the shares of the offerees who accepted`

#ASSERT (`By what day must the offeror pay or transfer the consideration to the offeree corporation` WITH `the day the offeror sent its notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21
#ASSERT `Did the offeror pay or transfer the consideration in time` WITH `the day the offeror sent its notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the offeror pay or transfer the consideration in time` WITH `the day the offeror sent its notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 22)
#ASSERT `Does the offeree corporation hold the money for me in trust` WITH `the offeree corporation has received the money or consideration from the offeror` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the offeree corporation hold the money for me in trust` WITH `the offeree corporation has received the money or consideration from the offeror` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Has the offeree corporation kept the money safe as the Act requires` WITH `the money is in a separate account` IS TRUE, `the bank's deposits are insured` IS TRUE, `other consideration is held in custody by a bank` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the offeree corporation kept the money safe as the Act requires` WITH `the money is in a separate account` IS TRUE, `the bank's deposits are insured` IS FALSE, `other consideration is held in custody by a bank` IS TRUE)
-- Case: where Quill itself makes the bid (a repurchase), it holds the money in trust and deposits it within 20 days.
#ASSERT `Does the corporation hold the money for me in trust when it is the one making the bid` WITH `the corporation is making a bid to repurchase all the shares of a class of its shares` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the corporation hold the money for me in trust when it is the one making the bid` WITH `the corporation is making a bid to repurchase all the shares of a class of its shares` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT (`By what day must the corporation deposit the money when it is the one making the bid` WITH `the day a notice was sent under section 206(3)` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21
#ASSERT `Did the corporation deposit the money in time when it is the one making the bid` WITH `the day a notice was sent under section 206(3)` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day the corporation deposited the money` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the corporation deposit the money in time when it is the one making the bid` WITH `the day a notice was sent under section 206(3)` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day the corporation deposited the money` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 22)

#ASSERT (`By what day must the offeree corporation act on the offeror's payment` WITH `the day the offeror sent its notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 7 31
#ASSERT `Did the offeree corporation act in time` WITH `the day the offeror sent its notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day the offeree corporation acted` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 31
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the offeree corporation act in time` WITH `the day the offeror sent its notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1, `the day the offeree corporation acted` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 1)
#ASSERT `Must the offeree corporation issue the offeror a share certificate for my shares` WITH `the offeror has paid or transferred what s 206(6) requires` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the offeree corporation issue the offeror a share certificate for my shares` WITH `the offeror has paid or transferred what s 206(6) requires` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the offeree corporation give me the money or consideration for my shares` WITH `I elected to accept the bid's terms` IS TRUE, `I sent my certificates as section 206(5)(a) requires` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the offeree corporation give me the money or consideration for my shares` WITH `I elected to accept the bid's terms` IS TRUE, `I sent my certificates as section 206(5)(a) requires` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the offeree corporation send me a notice that my shares were cancelled and the money is held for me` WITH `the offeror has paid or transferred what s 206(6) requires` IS TRUE, `the money is deposited as section 206(7) or 206(7.1) requires` IS TRUE, `I have not sent my certificates` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the offeree corporation send me a notice that my shares were cancelled and the money is held for me` WITH `the offeror has paid or transferred what s 206(6) requires` IS TRUE, `the money is deposited as section 206(7) or 206(7.1) requires` IS TRUE, `I have not sent my certificates` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the offeree corporation's notice to me say what the Act requires` WITH `it says my shares have been cancelled` IS TRUE, `it says the money is held in trust for me` IS TRUE, `it says it will send the money after receiving my shares` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the offeree corporation's notice to me say what the Act requires` WITH `it says my shares have been cancelled` IS TRUE, `it says the money is held in trust for me` IS FALSE, `it says it will send the money after receiving my shares` IS TRUE)

-- Case: Maya demands fair value; the offeror paid on 21 July 2026, so it may apply to a court until 10 August;
-- if it does not, Maya may apply from 11 to 30 August.
#ASSERT `May the offeror ask a court to fix the fair value of my shares` WITH `I elected to demand fair value` IS TRUE, `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21, `the day the offeror applied to the court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 10
#ASSERT NOT (`May the offeror ask a court to fix the fair value of my shares` WITH `I elected to demand fair value` IS TRUE, `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21, `the day the offeror applied to the court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 11)
#ASSERT (`By what day may the offeror ask a court to fix the fair value` WITH `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 8 10
#ASSERT `May I ask a court to fix the fair value of my shares myself` WITH `the offeror did not apply to a court` IS TRUE, `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21, `the day I apply to the court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 30
#ASSERT NOT (`May I ask a court to fix the fair value of my shares myself` WITH `the offeror did not apply to a court` IS TRUE, `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21, `the day I apply to the court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 31)
#ASSERT (`By what day may I ask a court to fix the fair value of my shares` WITH `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 8 30
#ASSERT (`Am I treated as having taken the bid's terms because no one applied to a court` WITH `no application was made to a court under section 206(10) in the period` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST `to transfer the shares on the terms on which the offeror acquired the shares of the offerees who accepted`
#ASSERT (`Am I treated as having taken the bid's terms because no one applied to a court` WITH `no application was made to a court under section 206(10) in the period` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is this the right court to apply to about take-over shares` WITH `it has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` IS TRUE, `it has jurisdiction in the province where I live` IS FALSE, `the corporation carries on business in my province` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this the right court to apply to about take-over shares` WITH `it has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` IS FALSE, `it has jurisdiction in the province where I live` IS TRUE, `the corporation carries on business in my province` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT (`Must I give security for costs when I apply to the court about take-over shares` WITH `the application is under section 206(9) or 206(10)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Must I give security for costs when I apply to the court about take-over shares` WITH `the application is under section 206(9) or 206(10)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Will I be a party to the court application about take-over shares and bound by its decision` WITH `I elected to demand fair value and the offeror has not acquired my shares` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Will I be a party to the court application about take-over shares and bound by its decision` WITH `I elected to demand fair value and the offeror has not acquired my shares` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Has the offeror told me what it must about the court application` WITH `the notice states the date` IS TRUE, `the notice states the place` IS TRUE, `the notice states the consequences` IS TRUE, `the notice states my right to appear and be heard` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the offeror told me what it must about the court application` WITH `the notice states the date` IS TRUE, `the notice states the place` IS FALSE, `the notice states the consequences` IS TRUE, `the notice states my right to appear and be heard` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Will the court fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting offerees together` WITH `an application has been made to a court` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the court fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting offerees together` WITH `an application has been made to a court` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the court appoint appraisers to help fix the fair value of my shares` WITH `an application has been made to a court` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court appoint appraisers to help fix the fair value of my shares` WITH `an application has been made to a court` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Will the court's final order be against the offeror and in my favour` WITH `the court has fixed a fair value` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the court's final order be against the offeror and in my favour` WITH `the court has fixed a fair value` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the court make this order in the proceedings about my shares` WITH `the court thinks the order fit` IS TRUE, `it is made in proceedings under section 206` IS TRUE, `the order` IS `an order that money payable to a shareholder who cannot be found be paid to the Receiver General, with subsection 227(3) applying (s 206(18)(d))`
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court make this order in the proceedings about my shares` WITH `the court thinks the order fit` IS FALSE, `it is made in proceedings under section 206` IS TRUE, `the order` IS `an order that money payable to a shareholder who cannot be found be paid to the Receiver General, with subsection 227(3) applying (s 206(18)(d))`)
#ASSERT `May the court allow interest on what I am owed for my take-over shares for the day I am asking about` WITH `the day I sent or delivered my certificates` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21, `the day of payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 31, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 15
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court allow interest on what I am owed for my take-over shares for the day I am asking about` WITH `the day I sent or delivered my certificates` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 21, `the day of payment` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 31, `the day I am asking about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 9 1)

-- Case: Omar never got the offeror's notice, and never received an offer; he learned of the bid on 20 June 2026
-- (the bid ended 1 June): his ninety days run from 20 June, to 18 September.
#ASSERT (`By what day may I require the offeror to buy my shares, because I never got its notice` WITH `I received an offer under the take-over bid` IS FALSE, `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day I learned of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 20) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 9 18
-- Had he received an offer, his ninety days would run from termination, to 30 August.
#ASSERT (`By what day may I require the offeror to buy my shares, because I never got its notice` WITH `I received an offer under the take-over bid` IS TRUE, `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day I learned of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 20) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 8 30
#ASSERT `May I require the offeror to buy my shares, because I never got its notice` WITH `I hold shares of a distributing corporation` IS TRUE, `I did not receive an offeror's notice under section 206(3)` IS TRUE, `I received an offer under the take-over bid` IS FALSE, `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day I learned of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 20, `the day I required the offeror to acquire my shares` IS YearMonthDay 2026 9 18
#ASSERT NOT (`May I require the offeror to buy my shares, because I never got its notice` WITH `I hold shares of a distributing corporation` IS TRUE, `I did not receive an offeror's notice under section 206(3)` IS TRUE, `I received an offer under the take-over bid` IS FALSE, `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day I learned of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 20, `the day I required the offeror to acquire my shares` IS YearMonthDay 2026 9 19)
#ASSERT NOT (`May I require the offeror to buy my shares, because I never got its notice` WITH `I hold shares of a distributing corporation` IS TRUE, `I did not receive an offeror's notice under section 206(3)` IS FALSE, `I received an offer under the take-over bid` IS FALSE, `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 1, `the day I learned of the take-over bid` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 20, `the day I required the offeror to acquire my shares` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT `Must the offeror buy my shares on the same terms as those who accepted` WITH `I have required the offeror to acquire my shares under section 206.1(1)` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the offeror buy my shares on the same terms as those who accepted` WITH `I have required the offeror to acquire my shares under section 206.1(1)` IS FALSE)



§§ `Winding up and reviving a corporation (Part XVIII, ss 207 to 213)`

-- Case: Harbour Mills Ltd. stopped trading, and its directors and shareholders (Priya, Tom and Wen) want to
-- wind it up. The corporation is solvent.
#ASSERT `Is this the right court for a dissolution application` WITH `the court has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this the right court for a dissolution application` WITH `the court has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Do the dissolution rules apply to my corporation if it is insolvent or bankrupt` WITH `the provision is section 209 or section 212` IS FALSE, `the corporation is an insolvent person as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS FALSE, `the corporation is a bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the dissolution rules apply to my corporation if it is insolvent or bankrupt` WITH `the provision is section 209 or section 212` IS FALSE, `the corporation is an insolvent person as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS TRUE, `the corporation is a bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the dissolution rules apply to my corporation if it is insolvent or bankrupt` WITH `the provision is section 209 or section 212` IS FALSE, `the corporation is an insolvent person as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS FALSE, `the corporation is a bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Do the dissolution rules apply to my corporation if it is insolvent or bankrupt` WITH `the provision is section 209 or section 212` IS TRUE, `the corporation is an insolvent person as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS TRUE, `the corporation is a bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the proceedings to dissolve my corporation stayed` WITH `proceedings are taken under this Part to dissolve or to liquidate and dissolve the corporation` IS TRUE, `the corporation is found in a proceeding under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act to be an insolvent person` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the proceedings to dissolve my corporation stayed` WITH `proceedings are taken under this Part to dissolve or to liquidate and dissolve the corporation` IS TRUE, `the corporation is found in a proceeding under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act to be an insolvent person` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the proceedings to dissolve my corporation stayed` WITH `proceedings are taken under this Part to dissolve or to liquidate and dissolve the corporation` IS FALSE, `the corporation is found in a proceeding under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act to be an insolvent person` IS TRUE)

-- Case: Harbour Mills was dissolved by the Director in 2024. Priya, a former creditor, asks to revive it.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to the Director to revive a dissolved body corporate` WITH `the way the body corporate was dissolved` IS `dissolved under this Part`, `I am an interested person` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to the Director to revive a dissolved body corporate` WITH `the way the body corporate was dissolved` IS `dissolved under section 268 of this Act`, `I am an interested person` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I apply to the Director to revive a dissolved body corporate` WITH `the way the body corporate was dissolved` IS `dissolved in some other way`, `I am an interested person` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I apply to the Director to revive a dissolved body corporate` WITH `the way the body corporate was dissolved` IS `dissolved under this Part`, `I am an interested person` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the Director issue me a certificate of revival` WITH `the Director has received articles of revival` IS TRUE, `the dissolved body corporate has fulfilled all conditions precedent that the Director considers reasonable` IS TRUE, `there is a valid reason for refusing to issue the certificate` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director issue me a certificate of revival` WITH `the Director has received articles of revival` IS FALSE, `the dissolved body corporate has fulfilled all conditions precedent that the Director considers reasonable` IS TRUE, `there is a valid reason for refusing to issue the certificate` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director issue me a certificate of revival` WITH `the Director has received articles of revival` IS TRUE, `the dissolved body corporate has fulfilled all conditions precedent that the Director considers reasonable` IS FALSE, `there is a valid reason for refusing to issue the certificate` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director issue me a certificate of revival` WITH `the Director has received articles of revival` IS TRUE, `the dissolved body corporate has fulfilled all conditions precedent that the Director considers reasonable` IS TRUE, `there is a valid reason for refusing to issue the certificate` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is the body corporate revived as a corporation on a given day` WITH `the date shown on the certificate of revival` IS YearMonthDay 2026 11 1, `the day asked about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 11 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the body corporate revived as a corporation on a given day` WITH `the date shown on the certificate of revival` IS YearMonthDay 2026 11 1, `the day asked about` IS YearMonthDay 2026 10 31)
#ASSERT `Is the revived corporation put back as it was in respect of a matter` WITH `the body corporate has been revived` IS TRUE, `the matter` IS `none of these`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the revived corporation put back as it was in respect of a matter` WITH `the body corporate has been revived` IS TRUE, `the matter` IS `a right acquired by a person after the dissolution`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the revived corporation put back as it was in respect of a matter` WITH `the body corporate has been revived` IS FALSE, `the matter` IS `none of these`)
#ASSERT `Is a legal action taken between dissolution and revival valid` WITH `the body corporate has been revived` IS TRUE, `the legal action respecting its affairs was taken between its dissolution and its revival` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a legal action taken between dissolution and revival valid` WITH `the body corporate has been revived` IS FALSE, `the legal action respecting its affairs was taken between its dissolution and its revival` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT (`Am I an "interested person" who can ask for revival` WITH `what I am to the dissolved body corporate` IS `a creditor of the dissolved body corporate (s 209(6)(a))`, `the contract is, in Quebec, a contract by gratuitous title` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Am I an "interested person" who can ask for revival` WITH `what I am to the dissolved body corporate` IS `a person who has a contract with the dissolved body corporate (s 209(6)(b))`, `the contract is, in Quebec, a contract by gratuitous title` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: a person the list does not name; the Act does not say either way.
#ASSERT (`Am I an "interested person" who can ask for revival` WITH `what I am to the dissolved body corporate` IS `a person not named in s 209(6)`, `the contract is, in Quebec, a contract by gratuitous title` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case: a corporation that never issued shares. The directors can end it at once.
#ASSERT `Can the directors alone dissolve a corporation that has never issued shares` WITH `the corporation has issued shares` IS FALSE, `all the directors have resolved to dissolve it` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the directors alone dissolve a corporation that has never issued shares` WITH `the corporation has issued shares` IS TRUE, `all the directors have resolved to dissolve it` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the directors alone dissolve a corporation that has never issued shares` WITH `the corporation has issued shares` IS FALSE, `all the directors have resolved to dissolve it` IS FALSE)

-- Case: no property and no liabilities; one class; 200 for and 100 against is exactly two thirds.
