#ASSERT `May the court order the distribution to be in money` WITH `I have applied under subsection 224(1)` IS TRUE, `the kind of order` IS `an order that the claims of the applying shareholder be satisfied by a distribution in money (s 224(2)(b))`
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court order the distribution to be in money` WITH `I have applied under subsection 224(1)` IS TRUE, `the kind of order` IS `an order of another kind than those s 224(2) names`)
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court order the distribution to be in money` WITH `I have applied under subsection 224(1)` IS FALSE, `the kind of order` IS `an order that all the property of the corporation be converted into and distributed in money (s 224(2)(a))`)
-- The prescribed period ends 31 December 2031; a shorter period fixed by order ends 30 June 2029.
#ASSERT (`By what day does a custodian of the records stay liable to produce them` WITH `the end of the prescribed period` IS YearMonthDay 2031 12 31, `the end of a shorter period fixed by an order made under subsection 223(5)` IS NOTHING) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2031 12 31
#ASSERT (`By what day does a custodian of the records stay liable to produce them` WITH `the end of the prescribed period` IS YearMonthDay 2031 12 31, `the end of a shorter period fixed by an order made under subsection 223(5)` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2029 6 30)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2029 6 30
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence if I fail to produce records I have custody of` WITH `I remain liable under subsection 225(1) and have not produced the documents and records` IS TRUE, `I have reasonable cause` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence if I fail to produce records I have custody of` WITH `I remain liable under subsection 225(1) and have not produced the documents and records` IS TRUE, `I have reasonable cause` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence if I fail to produce records I have custody of` WITH `I remain liable under subsection 225(1) and have not produced the documents and records` IS FALSE, `I have reasonable cause` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is this penalty within what the Act allows for failing to produce records` WITH `the fine in dollars` IS 5000, `the months of imprisonment` IS 6
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this penalty within what the Act allows for failing to produce records` WITH `the fine in dollars` IS 5001, `the months of imprisonment` IS 6)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this penalty within what the Act allows for failing to produce records` WITH `the fine in dollars` IS 5000, `the months of imprisonment` IS 7)



§§ `After dissolution (Part XVIII, ss 226 to 228)`

-- Case: Harbour Mills Ltd. was dissolved on 1 August 2026. Tom, a former shareholder, received 400 on the
-- distribution; a supplier is owed 1,000.
#ASSERT (`Does "shareholder" in the rules about dissolved corporations include me` WITH `what I am` IS `an heir of a shareholder`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Does "shareholder" in the rules about dissolved corporations include me` WITH `what I am` IS `a personal representative of a shareholder`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Does "shareholder" in the rules about dissolved corporations include me` WITH `what I am` IS `a shareholder, for the word shareholder in s 226(1)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not covered: a person who is none of these; the Act does not say.
#ASSERT (`Does "shareholder" in the rules about dissolved corporations include me` WITH `what I am` IS `a person who is not a shareholder, an heir or a personal representative (s 226(1))`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can a lawsuit begun before the corporation's dissolution go on` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved` IS TRUE, `the action or proceeding was commenced by or against the body corporate before its dissolution` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a lawsuit begun before the corporation's dissolution go on` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved` IS TRUE, `the action or proceeding was commenced by or against the body corporate before its dissolution` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a lawsuit begun before the corporation's dissolution go on` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved` IS FALSE, `the action or proceeding was commenced by or against the body corporate before its dissolution` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT (`By what day can someone still sue a dissolved corporation` WITH `the date of dissolution` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2028 8 1
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the dissolved corporation on a given day` WITH `the date of dissolution` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 1, `the day the action was brought` IS YearMonthDay 2028 8 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I still sue the dissolved corporation on a given day` WITH `the date of dissolution` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 1, `the day the action was brought` IS YearMonthDay 2028 8 2)
#ASSERT `Is the dissolved corporation's property still available to satisfy a judgment` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved` IS TRUE, `the property would have been available to satisfy the judgment or order if the body corporate had not been dissolved` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the dissolved corporation's property still available to satisfy a judgment` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved` IS TRUE, `the property would have been available to satisfy the judgment or order if the body corporate had not been dissolved` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the dissolved corporation's property still available to satisfy a judgment` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved` IS FALSE, `the property would have been available to satisfy the judgment or order if the body corporate had not been dissolved` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT (`Is service on this person service on a dissolved corporation` WITH `the person served is shown in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not covered: a person who is not so shown; the section does not say service on such a person fails.
#ASSERT (`Is service on this person service on a dissolved corporation` WITH `the person served is shown in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`How much can a shareholder who got the corporation's property be made to repay` WITH `a shareholder received property of the body corporate on a distribution` IS TRUE, `the person is claiming under subsection 226(2)` IS TRUE, `the amount the claimant is owed` IS 1000, `the amount received by the shareholder on the distribution` IS 400) EQUALS 400
#ASSERT (`How much can a shareholder who got the corporation's property be made to repay` WITH `a shareholder received property of the body corporate on a distribution` IS TRUE, `the person is claiming under subsection 226(2)` IS TRUE, `the amount the claimant is owed` IS 300, `the amount received by the shareholder on the distribution` IS 400) EQUALS 300
#ASSERT (`How much can a shareholder who got the corporation's property be made to repay` WITH `a shareholder received property of the body corporate on a distribution` IS FALSE, `the person is claiming under subsection 226(2)` IS TRUE, `the amount the claimant is owed` IS 1000, `the amount received by the shareholder on the distribution` IS 400) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Is a claim against a former shareholder brought in time` WITH `the date of dissolution` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 1, `the day the action was brought` IS YearMonthDay 2028 8 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a claim against a former shareholder brought in time` WITH `the date of dissolution` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 1, `the day the action was brought` IS YearMonthDay 2028 8 2)
#ASSERT `May a referee require a given contribution from me as a former shareholder` WITH `the plaintiff has established a claim in an action brought against the former shareholders as a class` IS TRUE, `the amount I received on the distribution` IS 400, `the amount the referee proposes I contribute` IS 400
#ASSERT NOT (`May a referee require a given contribution from me as a former shareholder` WITH `the plaintiff has established a claim in an action brought against the former shareholders as a class` IS TRUE, `the amount I received on the distribution` IS 400, `the amount the referee proposes I contribute` IS 401)
#ASSERT NOT (`May a referee require a given contribution from me as a former shareholder` WITH `the plaintiff has established a claim in an action brought against the former shareholders as a class` IS FALSE, `the amount I received on the distribution` IS 400, `the amount the referee proposes I contribute` IS 100)
#ASSERT `Must my share go to the Receiver General if I cannot be found` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS TRUE, `I, as a creditor or shareholder, cannot be found` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my share go to the Receiver General if I cannot be found` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS TRUE, `I, as a creditor or shareholder, cannot be found` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my share go to the Receiver General if I cannot be found` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS FALSE, `I, as a creditor or shareholder, cannot be found` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT (`How much will the Receiver General pay me if I prove my entitlement` WITH `the moneys paid to the Receiver General to which the person is entitled` IS 1250) EQUALS 1250
#ASSERT `Does the corporation's leftover property pass to the Crown on dissolution` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS TRUE, `the property had not been disposed of at the date of dissolution` IS TRUE, `the property remains available under subsection 226(2)` IS FALSE, `the property is the portion within section 227` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the corporation's leftover property pass to the Crown on dissolution` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS TRUE, `the property had not been disposed of at the date of dissolution` IS FALSE, `the property remains available under subsection 226(2)` IS FALSE, `the property is the portion within section 227` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the corporation's leftover property pass to the Crown on dissolution` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS TRUE, `the property had not been disposed of at the date of dissolution` IS TRUE, `the property remains available under subsection 226(2)` IS TRUE, `the property is the portion within section 227` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the corporation's leftover property pass to the Crown on dissolution` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS TRUE, `the property had not been disposed of at the date of dissolution` IS TRUE, `the property remains available under subsection 226(2)` IS FALSE, `the property is the portion within section 227` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the corporation's leftover property pass to the Crown on dissolution` WITH `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS FALSE, `the property had not been disposed of at the date of dissolution` IS TRUE, `the property remains available under subsection 226(2)` IS FALSE, `the property is the portion within section 227` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the revived corporation get its property back` WITH `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS TRUE, `the property is not money` IS TRUE, `the property vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` IS TRUE, `the property has not been disposed of` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the revived corporation get its property back` WITH `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS FALSE, `the property is not money` IS TRUE, `the property vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` IS TRUE, `the property has not been disposed of` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the revived corporation get its property back` WITH `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS TRUE, `the property is not money` IS FALSE, `the property vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` IS TRUE, `the property has not been disposed of` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the revived corporation get its property back` WITH `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS TRUE, `the property is not money` IS TRUE, `the property vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` IS FALSE, `the property has not been disposed of` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the revived corporation get its property back` WITH `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS TRUE, `the property is not money` IS TRUE, `the property vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` IS TRUE, `the property has not been disposed of` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT (`How much money does the revived corporation get back for money the Crown received` WITH `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS TRUE, `the money received by Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` IS 900) EQUALS 900
#ASSERT (`How much money does the revived corporation get back for money the Crown received` WITH `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS FALSE, `the money received by Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` IS 900) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`How much does the revived corporation get back for property the Crown has sold` WITH `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS TRUE, `property other than money vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1) and has been disposed of` IS TRUE, `the value of the property at the date it vested` IS 700, `the amount realized by Her Majesty from the disposition` IS 500) EQUALS 500
#ASSERT (`How much does the revived corporation get back for property the Crown has sold` WITH `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS TRUE, `property other than money vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1) and has been disposed of` IS TRUE, `the value of the property at the date it vested` IS 500, `the amount realized by Her Majesty from the disposition` IS 700) EQUALS 500
#ASSERT (`How much does the revived corporation get back for property the Crown has sold` WITH `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS TRUE, `property other than money vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1) and has been disposed of` IS FALSE, `the value of the property at the date it vested` IS 700, `the amount realized by Her Majesty from the disposition` IS 500) EQUALS 0

